#: lumos.fields.radiance:1 of
msgid "Spectral radiance maps of incoherent scenes (REQ-SIG-6)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`RadianceField` describes light that has no phase: the spectral "
"radiance :math:`L(x, y, \\lambda)` of a scene, optionally with the Stokes"
" parameters :math:`(I, Q, U, V)`, sampled at wavelengths "
":math:`\\lambda_k` on a :class:`~lumos.fields.Grid`. On an angular grid "
"(the sky) it is the radiance seen from the observer; on a spatial grid (a"
" laboratory source) it is the radiance leaving each point of the source "
"plane. Its data has shape ``(nλ, ny, nx)`` or ``(nλ, 4, ny, nx)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance:10 of
msgid "Radiometric units"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance:11 of
msgid ""
"The radiance may be given per wavelength or per frequency, in energy or "
"photon units, e.g. ``W m⁻² sr⁻¹ m⁻¹``, ``photon s⁻¹ m⁻² sr⁻¹ m⁻¹``, ``erg"
" s⁻¹ cm⁻² sr⁻¹ Å⁻¹`` or ``Jy sr⁻¹``. Conversions use the wavelength of "
"each channel (Rybicki & Lightman, *Radiative Processes in Astrophysics*, "
"§1.3):"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance:15 of
msgid ""
"L_\\lambda = L_\\nu \\frac{c}{\\lambda^2}, \\qquad L^{\\mathrm{ph}} = L "
"\\frac{\\lambda}{h c} .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance:17 of
msgid ""
"Pixels are piecewise-constant: :meth:`RadianceField.resample` computes "
"each new pixel as the area-weighted mean of the old pixels it overlaps, "
"which conserves the flux :math:`\\sum L\\,\\Delta A` (§9 of the "
"specifications)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.CANONICAL_RADIANCE:1 of
msgid "Canonical SI spectral radiance, per wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField:1 of
msgid "Spectral radiance of an incoherent scene sampled on a grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField:3 of
msgid ""
"Spectral radiance, a quantity of shape ``(nλ, ny, nx)`` or ``(nλ, 4, ny, "
"nx)`` (Stokes I, Q, U, V)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField:4 of
msgid "Angular (sky) or spatial (source plane) sampling."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField:5 of
msgid "``nλ`` vacuum wavelengths of the channels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField:7 of
msgid "Values of the radiance in :attr:`unit`, as a real backend array."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.data:1 of
msgid "Radiance values in :attr:`unit` (real backend array)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.radiance:1 of
msgid "Radiance as a NumPy quantity in :attr:`unit`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.unit:1 of
msgid "Unit of :attr:`data`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.wavelengths:1 of
msgid "Wavelengths of the channels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.wavelengths_si:1 of
msgid "Wavelengths in metres."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.has_stokes:1 of
msgid "Whether the data holds the four Stokes parameters along axis 1."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.shape:1 of
msgid "Shape of :attr:`data`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.backend:1 of
msgid "Name of the backend holding the data."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.to:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the same radiance expressed in ``unit`` (per wavelength or "
"frequency, energy or photons)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.integrated:1 of
msgid ""
"Return :math:`\\sum L\\,\\Delta A` per wavelength (Stokes I only), shape "
"``(nλ,)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.integrated:3 of
msgid ""
"On an angular grid it is the spectral irradiance at the observer (e.g. W "
"m⁻² m⁻¹); on a spatial grid it is the spectral radiant intensity of the "
"source (e.g. W sr⁻¹ m⁻¹)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.resample:1 of
msgid ""
"Resample onto ``grid`` by area-weighted averaging, conserving the flux "
"inside the overlap."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.to_backend:1 of
msgid "Return the same radiance held by backend ``name``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.to_json:1 of
msgid "Encode the radiance field as a strict-JSON-compatible dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal:1 of
msgid "Modal amplitudes of the light in one guide (REQ-SIG-7, ADR-0023)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`ModalField` is one *guided lane*: the complex amplitudes "
":math:`a_j` of the light in the :math:`n` modes of one guide (``n = 1`` "
"for a single-mode guide) at the wavelengths :math:`\\lambda_k`, for "
":math:`M` mutually incoherent sources. Its array has shape ``(nλ, n)`` or"
" ``(M, nλ, n)``, and :math:`|a_j|^2` is the power in mode :math:`j` (in "
":attr:`ModalField.power_unit`). Guides separated in space are the lanes "
"of a :class:`~lumos.fields.Bus`, never modes of one field."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal:9 of
msgid ""
":attr:`ModalField.sources` identifies the source list the sources come "
"from: lanes interfere only if they describe the same sources in the same "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal:12 of
msgid ""
"Scattering matrices (:mod:`lumos.fields.smatrix`) act with "
":meth:`ModalField.apply`. Incoherent sources add in power and spectral "
"channels add with the weights :math:`w_k`, like "
":class:`~lumos.fields.Wavecube`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField:1 of
msgid "Complex amplitudes of the modes of one guide at several wavelengths."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField:3 of
msgid ""
"Complex amplitudes, shape ``(nλ, n)`` or ``(M, nλ, n)`` (``n`` modes, "
"``M`` incoherent sources)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField:4 of
msgid "``nλ`` vacuum wavelengths."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField:5 of
msgid "Spectral weights for :attr:`detected_power` (default: ones)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField:6 of
msgid "Optional names of the ``n`` modes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField:7 of
msgid ""
"``u.W`` (default) or ``u.photon / u.s``: :math:`|a|^2` is a power in this"
" unit."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField:8 of
msgid ""
"Identifier of the source list the ``M`` sources come from (``None``: "
"unknown)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.amplitudes:1 of
msgid ""
"Complex amplitudes, a backend array of shape ``(nλ, n)`` or ``(M, nλ, "
"n)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.shape:1 of
msgid "Shape of :attr:`amplitudes`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.n_sources:1 of
msgid "Number of incoherent sources ``M`` (1 without a source axis)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.n_modes:1 of
msgid "Number of guided modes ``n``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.wavelengths:1 of
msgid "Vacuum wavelengths."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.weights:1 of
msgid "Spectral weights (a copy)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.labels:1 of
msgid "Names of the modes, if given."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.sources:1 of
msgid "Identifier of the source list described by the source axis, or ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.power_unit:1 of
msgid "Unit of :math:`|a|^2`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.backend:1 of
msgid "Name of the backend holding the amplitudes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.mode_power:1 of
msgid ""
"Power per wavelength and mode, summed over the incoherent sources, shape "
"``(nλ, n)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.total_power:1 of
msgid "Power summed over the modes, per wavelength, shape ``(nλ,)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.detected_power:1 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Spectrally weighted power per mode :math:`\\sum_k w_k P_{kj}`, shape "
"``(n,)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.apply:1 of
msgid ""
"Apply a scattering matrix ``(n_out, n_in)`` or ``(nλ, n_out, n_in)`` to "
"each source and wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.apply:3 of
msgid ""
"``labels`` names the output modes (the input labels are kept for a square"
" matrix by default)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.to_backend:1 of
msgid "Return the same amplitudes held by backend ``name``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.to_json:1 of
msgid "Encode the modal field as a strict-JSON-compatible dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus:1 of
msgid "Buses: N lanes of the same kind of signal, separated in space (ADR-0023)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`Bus` groups the signals of guides or beams that are separated "
"in space, so that different components can be placed on each of them: the"
" waveguides of a photonic chip, the arms of an interferometer. Each "
"*lane* is one signal: a guided lane is a "
":class:`~lumos.fields.ModalField` of one guide (its modes), a free-space "
"lane a :class:`~lumos.fields.Wavefront`, :class:`~lumos.fields.Wavecube` "
"or :class:`~lumos.fields.IncoherentBundle`. Spectral channels, incoherent"
" sources and the modes of one guide are never lanes: they share the same "
"beam or guide."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus:10 of
msgid ""
"A bus behaves as a sequence (``len(bus)``, ``bus[i]``, iteration) and "
"names its lanes (``T1``, ``T2``... by default); it may also carry the "
"projected position of the telescope feeding each lane."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus:14 of
msgid "Implicit packing"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus:15 of
msgid ""
"When its lanes share their metadata, a bus stores them in one array, so "
"that a component acting on all the lanes works on that array without "
"copying them:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus:18 of
msgid ""
"guided lanes with the same sources, wavelengths, spectral weights and "
"power unit are concatenated along the mode axis, ``(sources, λ, Σ "
"modes)``, the lanes possibly having different numbers of modes "
"(:attr:`Bus.modal`, :attr:`Bus.mode_counts`);"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus:21 of
msgid ""
"free-space lanes of the same class with identical metadata (grid, "
"sources, wavelengths, weights, polarisation, power unit) and shape are "
"stacked, ``(lanes, *lane_shape)`` (:attr:`Bus.field`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus:24 of
msgid ""
"Otherwise the bus keeps the list of its lanes; "
":meth:`Bus.packing_problem` says why. Both forms have the same interface."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus:1 of
msgid ""
"N lanes of the same signal class, separated in space, packed in one array"
" when possible."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus:3 of
msgid ""
"The signals of the lanes, all of the same class (``ModalField``, "
"``Wavefront``, ``Wavecube`` or ``IncoherentBundle``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus:5 of
msgid "Names of the lanes (default ``T1``... ``Tn``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus:6 of
msgid ""
"Projected positions ``(x, y)`` of the telescopes feeding the lanes, shape"
" ``(N, 2)``, as a length quantity; ``NaN`` rows for unknown positions."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus:8 of
msgid ""
"Store the lanes in one array when they share their metadata (default). "
"``False`` keeps a list, which behaves the same."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.guided:1 of
msgid "Build a packed bus of guided lanes from the amplitudes of all their modes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.guided:3 of
msgid ""
"``amplitudes`` has the shape ``(nλ, Σ modes)`` or ``(sources, nλ, Σ "
"modes)``; ``modes`` gives the number of modes of each lane (default: one "
"single-mode lane per column). ``labels`` name the modes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.packing_problem:1 of
msgid ""
"Return why ``lanes`` cannot be packed in one array, or ``None`` if they "
"can."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.n_lanes:1 of
msgid "Number of lanes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.lanes:1 of
msgid "The signals of the lanes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.names:1 of
msgid "Names of the lanes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.positions:1 of
msgid ""
"Projected positions of the telescopes feeding the lanes, ``(N, 2)``, or "
"``None``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.lane_type:1 of
msgid "Signal class of the lanes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.packed:1 of
msgid "Whether the lanes are stored in one array."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.backend:1 of
msgid "Name of the backend holding the lanes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.sources:1 of
msgid "Identifier of the source list shared by every lane, or ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.mode_counts:1 of
msgid "Number of modes of each guided lane."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.modal:1 of
msgid ""
"All the modes of all the lanes of a packed guided bus, ``(sources, λ, Σ "
"modes)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.with_modal:1 of
msgid ""
"Return a packed guided bus of the modes ``modal``, lanes of ``counts`` "
"modes named ``names``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.with_modal:3 of
msgid "Positions are kept for the lanes whose name is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.field:1 of
msgid ""
"Stacked arrays of the lanes of a packed free-space bus, ``(lanes, "
"*lane_shape)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.select:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the bus of the lanes ``indices``, in this order, with their names "
"and positions."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.concatenate:1 of
msgid ""
"Put the lanes of ``buses`` side by side (packed again when possible), "
"without mixing them."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.map:1 of
msgid ""
"Apply ``function`` (lane -> lane) to every lane; names and positions are "
"kept."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.to_backend:1 of
msgid "Return the same lanes held by backend ``name``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.bus.Bus.to_json:1 of
msgid ""
"Encode the bus as a strict-JSON-compatible dictionary (lanes listed one "
"by one)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.dataproduct:1 of
msgid ""
"Detected and processed data with units, axes, mask and uncertainties "
"(REQ-SIG-9)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.dataproduct:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`DataProduct` is what a detector or a processing block produces:"
" an image, a cube, a time series or scalars. It carries"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.dataproduct:6 of
msgid "``data``: a NumPy quantity (``adu``, ``electron``, ``photon``, ``W``...);"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.dataproduct:7 of
msgid ""
"``axes``: one named 1D coordinate quantity per data axis (pixels by "
"default);"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.dataproduct:8 of
msgid "``mask``: optional booleans, ``True`` for invalid samples;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.dataproduct:9 of
msgid "``uncertainty``: optional standard deviations, in the unit of the data;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.dataproduct:10 of
msgid ""
"``meta``: acquisition metadata (strings, numbers, booleans, quantities, "
"lists of them)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.dataproduct:12 of
msgid ""
"Sums and differences of independent products add their uncertainties in "
"quadrature, and scaling by a constant scales the uncertainty by its "
"absolute value (JCGM 100:2008, *GUM*, §5.1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/index.md:126 lumos.fields.dataproduct:16 of
