#: lumos.fields.smatrix:1 of
msgid "Scattering matrices of guided-wave components (REQ-SIG-7)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A component with :math:`n_\\mathrm{in}` input and :math:`n_\\mathrm{out}`"
" output channels maps the modal amplitudes :math:`a` to :math:`S a`, with"
" :math:`S` of shape ``(n_out, n_in)`` or, for a wavelength-dependent "
"component, ``(nλ, n_out, n_in)``. Lossless reciprocal components have "
"unitary matrices, :math:`S^\\dagger S = 1` (Pozar, *Microwave "
"Engineering*, §4.3), and conserve the power."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix:8 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Phases follow the :math:`e^{-i\\omega t}` convention of §9 of the "
"specifications: :math:`e^{+i\\phi}` is a delay."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.coupler:1 of
msgid ""
"Symmetric lossless directional coupler with power coupling ratio "
"``ratio`` (``κ²``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.coupler:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"S = \\begin{pmatrix} t & i\\kappa \\\\ i\\kappa & t \\end{pmatrix}, "
"\\qquad t = \\sqrt{1 - \\kappa^2}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.coupler:5 of
msgid ""
"(Okamoto, *Fundamentals of Optical Waveguides*, §4.4). ``ratio = 0.5`` is"
" the 50/50 coupler."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.is_unitary:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether a square matrix (or every matrix of a stack) satisfies ``S^† S = "
"1`` within ``atol``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.phase_shifter:1 of
msgid "Diagonal matrix applying the phase ``phases[j]`` to channel ``j``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:1 of
msgid "Sampling of a spectral band for polychromatic computations (REQ-SIG-4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:3 of
msgid ""
"A polychromatic quantity is integrated over a band with a quadrature "
"rule: wavelengths :math:`\\lambda_k` and weights :math:`w_k` such that"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:6 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\frac{1}{\\Delta\\lambda}\\int_{\\lambda_0 - "
"\\Delta\\lambda/2}^{\\lambda_0 + \\Delta\\lambda/2}\n"
"f(\\lambda)\\,d\\lambda \\approx \\sum_k w_k f(\\lambda_k), \\qquad "
"\\sum_k w_k = 1 .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:9 of
msgid ""
"``\"midpoint\"``: ``n`` equal panels sampled at their centres, equal "
"weights ``1/n``; exact for linear spectra, robust for any spectrum."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:11 of
msgid ""
"``\"gauss\"``: Gauss-Legendre nodes and weights; exact for polynomials of"
" degree ``2n - 1``, the most accurate choice for smooth spectra."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:1 of
msgid "Return wavelengths and normalised weights sampling a band."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:3 of
msgid "Central wavelength of the band."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:4 of
msgid "Full width of the band; the band must stay at positive wavelengths."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:5 of
msgid "Number of samples."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:6 of
msgid "``\"midpoint\"`` or ``\"gauss\"`` (Gauss-Legendre)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:8 of
msgid ""
"* **wavelengths** (*astropy.units.Quantity*) -- ``n`` wavelengths in the "
"unit of ``center``. * **weights** (*numpy.ndarray*) -- ``n`` weights "
"summing to 1 (band average)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:8 of
msgid ""
"**wavelengths** (*astropy.units.Quantity*) -- ``n`` wavelengths in the "
"unit of ``center``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:9 of
msgid ""
"**weights** (*numpy.ndarray*) -- ``n`` weights summing to 1 (band "
"average)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:1 of
msgid ""
"Polarisation: Jones vectors, Jones matrices and Stokes parameters (REQ-"
"SIG-3)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:3 of
msgid ""
"A polarised :class:`~lumos.fields.Wavefront` holds the Jones components "
":math:`(E_x, E_y)` in the laboratory basis along the first axis of its "
"field, of shape ``(2, ny, nx)``. Polarising elements multiply it by a "
":math:`2 \\times 2` Jones matrix, uniform (shape ``(2, 2)``) or varying "
"across the grid (shape ``(2, 2, ny, nx)``), with :func:`apply`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:9 of
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:10 of
msgid "Angles are measured from +x towards +y."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:11 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With the time dependence :math:`e^{-i\\omega t}` of §9 of the "
"specifications, a phase factor :math:`e^{+i\\phi}` is a delay. A retarder"
" of retardance :math:`\\Gamma` with its fast axis along x is "
":math:`\\mathrm{diag}(1, e^{i\\Gamma})`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:14 of
msgid "Stokes parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:16 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"S_0 = |E_x|^2 + |E_y|^2,\\quad S_1 = |E_x|^2 - |E_y|^2,\\quad\n"
"S_2 = 2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(E_x^* E_y),\\quad S_3 = 2\\,\\mathrm{Im}(E_x^* "
"E_y).\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:19 of
msgid ""
"The right circular state :math:`R = (1, i)/\\sqrt 2` turns clockwise for "
"an observer facing the source and has :math:`S_3 = +S_0` (Born & Wolf, "
"*Principles of Optics*, §1.4.2)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.apply:1 of
msgid ""
"Apply a Jones matrix to a polarised wavefront, wavecube (every channel) "
"or bundle (every mode)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.apply:3 of
msgid ""
"Shape ``(2, 2)`` (uniform) or ``(2, 2, ny, nx)`` (varying across the "
"grid), any backend."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.apply:4 of
msgid ""
"Polarised :class:`~lumos.fields.Wavefront` (field ``(2, ny, nx)``) or "
":class:`~lumos.fields.Wavecube` (field ``(nλ, 2, ny, nx)``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.degree_of_polarization:1 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Return :math:`\\sqrt{S_1^2 + S_2^2 + S_3^2} / S_0` for Stokes parameters "
"along the first axis."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.half_wave_plate:1 of
msgid "Half-wave plate (retardance π) with its fast axis at ``angle``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.linear:1 of
msgid "Return the Jones vector of a linear polarisation at ``angle`` from x."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.polarizer:1 of
msgid ""
"Ideal linear polariser transmitting the polarisation at ``angle`` (a "
"projector)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.quarter_wave_plate:1 of
msgid "Quarter-wave plate (retardance π/2) with its fast axis at ``angle``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.retarder:1 of
msgid ""
"Linear retarder of retardance :math:`\\Gamma` with its fast axis at "
"``angle``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.retarder:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The slow axis is delayed by :math:`e^{i\\Gamma}`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.rotator:1 of
msgid ""
"Polarisation rotator turning every linear polarisation by ``angle`` (e.g."
" a Faraday rotator)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.stokes:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the Stokes parameters ``(S0, S1, S2, S3)``, shape ``(4, ny, nx)`` "
"or ``(nλ, 4, ny, nx)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.stokes:3 of
msgid ""
"They are in the intensity unit of the signal. For an "
":class:`~lumos.fields.IncoherentBundle`, the Stokes parameters of the "
"modes add with the mode weights (incoherent superposition, Born & Wolf "
"§10.8.3), which describes partially polarised and natural light."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.vector:1 of
msgid "Return the normalised Jones vector of a basis state."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.vector:3 of
msgid ""
"``\"H\"`` (horizontal, x), ``\"V\"`` (vertical, y), ``\"D\"`` (diagonal, "
"+45°), ``\"A\"`` (anti-diagonal, -45°), ``\"R\"`` (right circular) or "
"``\"L\"`` (left circular)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/index.md:98
msgid "Contexts and graphs"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context:1 of
msgid "Container and coordinator of elements."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context:3 of
msgid "``\"simulation\"`` (default) or ``\"operation\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context:4 of
msgid ""
"Whether the digital twin runs alongside the real equipment in operation "
"mode (default ``True``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context:5 of
msgid ""
"Array backend used by :meth:`run`: ``\"auto\"`` (default, the process "
"default) or a backend name."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context:6 of
msgid ""
"Seed of the random streams; a random 32-bit seed is drawn (and kept) if "
"``None``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context:7 of
msgid ""
"Absolute start date of the clock (``astropy.time.Time``, UTC); defaults "
"to now."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context:8 of
msgid "Optional name of the context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.mode:1 of
msgid "``\"simulation\"`` or ``\"operation\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.mode:3 of
msgid "Operating mode"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.twin:1 of
msgid "Whether the digital twin is enabled in operation mode."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.backend:1 of
msgid "the process default)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.backend:3 of
msgid "Backend used by :meth:`run` (``\"auto\"``"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.graph:1 of
msgid "The graph of elements."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.add:1 of
msgid "Add elements and return them (the element itself when only one is given)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.add:3 of
msgid ""
"``id`` sets the identifier of a single element (by default its name, or "
"its class name and a counter)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.remove:1 lumos.core.graph.Graph.remove:1 of
msgid "Remove ``element`` and its connections."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.disconnect:1 of
msgid "Remove the connection ``source`` → ``target``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.connect:1 of
msgid ""
"Connect an output port to an input port (adding the target element if "
"needed)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.id_of:1 of
msgid "Return the identifier of ``element`` in the context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.elements:1 of
msgid "Elements by identifier."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.port:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the port ``\"element.port\"`` (``\"group.child.port\"`` inside "
"groups)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.run:1 of
msgid ""
"Compute the requested outputs (ports, elements or ``\"id.port\"`` "
"strings), see :meth:`Graph.run`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.run:3 of
msgid ""
"Records of the LUMOS loggers emitted during the run (numerical choices, "
"physical warnings) are copied to the journal."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.run:6 of
msgid "Output ports, elements or ``\"id.port\"`` strings."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.run:7 of
msgid ""
"``True`` or a name: write an archive of the run "
"(:func:`lumos.results.new_archive`) holding the context, the metadata, "
"the journal and the computed outputs (in ``data/<id.port>``); it is "
"returned as ``result.archive``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.run:10 of
msgid ""
"Directory of the archive (default: next to the executed script or "
"notebook)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.run:11 of
msgid "Called as ``progress(done, total, element_id)`` after each element."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.record:1 of
msgid ""
"Record the actions of the block: ``with ctx.record() as sequence: ...`` "
"(REQ-HW-7)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.replay:1 of
msgid ""
"Execute the actions of a recorded sequence in the current mode; return "
"their results."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.link:1 of
msgid ""
"Make the field ``target`` follow the field ``source`` (paths "
"``\"element.field\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.link:3 of
msgid ""
"``target = offset + scale * source``, or ``function(source)``: a stage "
"carrying a lens drives a propagation distance, a phase controller drives "
"phase shifters. Links are applied after every action and before every "
"run, so that the digital twin follows the bench."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.apply_links:1 of
msgid "Copy the linked fields to their targets."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.origin:1 lumos.core.journal.JournalEntry:10 of
msgid "``\"python\"``, ``\"web\"`` or ``\"mcp\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.origin:3 of
msgid "Origin of the actions being executed"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.as_origin:1 of
msgid "Attribute the actions of the block to ``origin`` in the journal."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.time:1 of
msgid "Current absolute date of the clock."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.elapsed:1 of
msgid "Time elapsed since the start of the clock."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.wait:1 of
msgid ""
"Let ``duration`` pass (counts as one duration inside a :meth:`parallel` "
"block)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.parallel:1 of
msgid ""
"Run the actions of the block simultaneously: the clock advances by the "
"longest duration."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.seed:1 of
msgid ""
"Seed of the random streams; changing it recomputes the stochastic "
"elements."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.realization:1 of
msgid ""
"Index of the noise realization (0 by default); changing it recomputes the"
" stochastic elements."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.realization:3 of
msgid ""
"Every realization gives independent random streams, reproducible with the"
" same seed: Monte-Carlo runs draw realization ``k`` at their ``k``-th "
"point (see :meth:`sample`). Realization 0 gives the streams of the seed "
"alone."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.walk:1 of
msgid ""
"Every element of the context with its path, including the children of "
"groups."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.simulate:1 of
msgid ""
"Force ``element`` to simulation, even in operation mode (``flag=False`` "
"removes the override)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.mode_of:1 of
msgid ""
"Effective mode of ``element``: the context mode unless the element is "
"forced to simulation."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.path_of:1 of
msgid "Path of ``element`` from the context: ``\"id\"`` or ``\"group.child\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.drivers:1 of
msgid "Drivers attached to the elements, by element path."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.stop_all:1 of
msgid ""
"Emergency stop: stop every driver, then bring the equipment to its safe "
"state (REQ-HW-4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.operation_guard:1 of
msgid ""
"Run a block of operations; on ``KeyboardInterrupt`` or any error, stop "
"everything and secure it."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.twin_state:1 of
msgid ""
"State measured on the equipment at the last command, next to the twin's "
"simulated state."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.spawn_key:1 of
msgid ""
"Spawn key of the random stream of an element (or identifier): the UTF-8 "
"bytes of its path."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.spawn_key:3 of
msgid ""
"The path is the identifier of a top-level element and ``\"group.child\"``"
" inside groups. For a noise realization ``r > 0`` (:attr:`realization`), "
"the key ends with ``0xFF, r``: ``0xFF`` never occurs in UTF-8, so the "
"streams of different paths and realizations are independent."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.rng:1 of
msgid ""
"Return a new generator of the reproducible random stream of an element "
"(or identifier)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.rng:3 of
msgid ""
"Streams derive from ``numpy.random.SeedSequence(seed, spawn_key=...)``: "
"they are independent between elements and noise realizations, and "
"identical between runs with the same seed and realization."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sweep:1 of
msgid "Run the context for several values of some fields and collect the outputs."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sweep:3 of
msgid ""
"Values of each field, by path ``\"element.field\"`` "
"(``\"group.child.field\"`` inside groups)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sweep:4 of
msgid "Outputs to compute at each point (see :meth:`run`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sweep:5 of
msgid ""
"``\"grid\"``: every combination (Cartesian product, last parameter "
"varying fastest); ``\"zip\"``: the i-th values of every parameter "
"together."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sweep:7 of
msgid ""
"``\"fixed\"`` (default): every point has the noise of the context, so "
"that the points differ by their parameters only (common random numbers); "
"``\"independent\"``: point ``k`` (from 1) draws the noise realization "
"``k`` (:attr:`realization`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sweep:10 of
msgid ""
"Called as ``progress(done, total)`` after each point; it may raise to "
"stop the sweep."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sweep:12 of
msgid ""
"One point per combination. The fields and the realization get their "
"values back afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.Context.feedbacks:1 of
msgid "The feedbacks of the loops of the context, in the order they are applied."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.feedback:1 of
msgid ""
"Feed the value of the output port ``source`` back to the field ``target``"
" between iterations."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.feedback:3 of
msgid ""
"The graph of signals stays acyclic: feedbacks are applied by :meth:`loop`"
" after each iteration, so a loop has a delay of one period. With "
"``mode=\"add\"`` the value is added to the field (an integrator whose "
"gain is in the element computing the correction); with ``\"set\"`` it "
"replaces it. The source element may refuse a target (method "
"``check_feedback(element, field)``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.remove_feedback:1
#: lumos.service.service.Service.remove_feedback:1 of
msgid "Remove the feedback from ``source`` to ``target``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.loop:1 of
msgid ""
"Run the context as a closed loop: ``steps`` iterations of ``period`` "
"(REQ-CTX-2, ADR-0020)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.loop:3 of
msgid ""
"Iteration ``k`` computes ``outputs`` (and the sources of the feedbacks) "
"at the elapsed time ``t_0 + k·period``, applies the feedbacks, then "
"advances the clock by ``period``: a correction computed from a "
"measurement acts on the next iteration."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.loop:7 of
msgid "Number of iterations."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.loop:8 of
msgid "Duration of an iteration (a time quantity)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.loop:9 of
msgid "Outputs to compute and return at each iteration (see :meth:`run`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.loop:10 of
msgid ""
"Put back the fields driven by the feedbacks and the clock afterwards "
"(default: keep them, the loop has run)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.loop:12 of
msgid ""
"Called as ``progress(done, steps)`` after each iteration; it may raise to"
" stop the loop."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.free_parameters:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the priors of the free parameters, by path ``\"element.field\"`` "
"(``None`` without prior)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sample:1 of
msgid ""
"Monte-Carlo run: draw ``n`` values of every free parameter from its prior"
" and run the context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sample:3 of
msgid ""
"Draws come from the reproducible stream ``ctx.rng(\"sample\")`` of the "
"current realization, parameter after parameter in the order of "
":meth:`free_parameters`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sample:6 of
msgid "Number of draws."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sample:7 of
msgid "Outputs to compute at each draw (see :meth:`run`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sample:8 of
msgid ""
"``\"independent\"`` (default): draw ``k`` (from 1) also draws the noise "
"realization ``k`` of the stochastic elements, so that the spread of the "
"outputs includes the noise; without free parameters the run is repeated "
"with independent noise. ``\"fixed\"``: every draw has the noise of the "
"context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.sample:11 of
msgid ""
"Called as ``progress(done, n)`` after each draw; it may raise to stop the"
" run."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Context.to_python:1 of
msgid ""
"Return a Python script rebuilding this context (see "
":func:`lumos.io.codegen.to_python`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context:1 of
msgid "The context: container and coordinator of a LUMOS system (``REQ-CTX-*``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`Context` holds the graph of elements and everything that is "
"global to a simulation or an experiment: the operating mode (simulation "
"or operation) and the digital twin (REQ-EL-4, REQ-EL-7), the array "
"backend, the observation settings (spectral band, site, pointing; REQ-"
"CTX-6) and the random seed from which every element gets its own "
"reproducible random stream."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Observation:1 of
msgid "Observation settings shared by the elements of a context (REQ-CTX-6)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Observation:3 of
msgid "``(min, max)`` wavelengths of the spectral band, or ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Observation:4 of
msgid "Number of spectral samples of the band."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Observation:5 of
msgid ""
"Quadrature rule of the band, ``\"midpoint\"`` or ``\"gauss\"`` "
"(:func:`lumos.fields.spectral_samples`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Observation:6 of
msgid "Free-form JSON-compatible settings (site, platform, pointing...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Observation.band:1 of
msgid "Spectral band ``(min, max)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.Observation.wavelengths:1 of
msgid "Return the wavelengths and normalised weights sampling the band."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.SweepPoint:1 of
msgid "One point of a sweep or Monte-Carlo run."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.SweepPoint:3 of
msgid "Values of the swept or drawn fields, by path ``\"element.field\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.SweepPoint:5 of
msgid "The computed outputs."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.context.SweepPoint:7 of
msgid ""
"Noise realization of the run (:attr:`Context.realization`; 0 for the "
"noise of the context)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph:1 of
msgid ""
"Directed acyclic graph of elements connected port to port, with pull "
"execution (REQ-CTX-1/2/4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`Graph` holds elements under unique identifiers and the "
"connections between their ports. A connection goes from an output port to"
" an input port whose signal type is the same or a base class (REQ-"
"SIG-11). The graph is acyclic: physical loops (adaptive optics, servo "
"loops, iterative calibration) are iterations in time driven by the "
"context, not cycles of signals."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph:8 of
msgid ""
"Execution is *pull*: :meth:`Graph.run` computes only the elements needed "
"by the requested outputs, in topological order. The outputs of every "
"element are cached; changing a parameter or a state of an element, or a "
"connection, invalidates the cache of that element and of everything "
"downstream."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Connection:1 of
msgid "A connection from an output port to an input port."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.CycleError:1 of
msgid "Raised when a connection would create a cycle."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph:1 of
msgid "Elements and their connections."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.add:1 of
msgid "Add ``element`` and return its identifier."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.add:3 of
msgid ""
"The identifier is ``id`` if given, otherwise the element name, otherwise "
"the lower-case class name followed by a counter."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.id_of:1 of
msgid "Return the identifier of ``element`` in this graph."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.elements:1 of
msgid "Elements by identifier (a copy)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.connections:1 of
msgid "Connections in creation order (a copy)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.connect:1 of
msgid "Connect the output ``source`` to the input ``target``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.connect:3 of
msgid "If the directions or signal types are incompatible."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.connect:4 of
msgid "If an element is not in the graph or a single input is already connected."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.connect:5 of
msgid "If the connection would create a cycle."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.disconnect:1 of
msgid "Remove the connection from ``source`` to ``target``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.incoming:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the connections arriving at the input ``target``, in creation "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.upstream:1 of
msgid ""
"Elements feeding ``element`` directly, in connection order, without "
"duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.downstream:1 of
msgid ""
"Elements fed directly by ``element``, in connection order, without "
"duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.topological_order:1 of
msgid ""
"Elements ordered so that every connection goes forward (Kahn's algorithm,"
" stable)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.required:1 of
msgid ""
"Elements needed to compute ``targets`` (elements or output ports), in "
"topological order."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.invalidate:1 of
msgid ""
"Drop the cached outputs of ``element`` and everything downstream "
"(everything if ``None``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.is_cached:1 of
msgid "Whether the outputs of ``element`` are cached."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.resolve:1 of
msgid ""
"Turn ``\"id\"`` or ``\"id.port\"`` into an element or a port reference; "
"other values pass through."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.run:1 of
msgid "Compute the requested outputs."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.run:3 of
msgid ""
"Output ports, elements (all their outputs) or identifiers ``\"id\"`` / "
"``\"id.port\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.run:4 of
msgid ""
"Signals given directly to unconnected input ports (used by groups for "
"their exposed inputs). The caller invalidates the elements whose feeds "
"changed."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.run:6 of
msgid ""
"Called as ``progress(done, total, element_id)`` after each element (for "
"long runs)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Graph.run:8 of
msgid "The signals by output port, also reachable by ``\"id.port\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.GraphError:1 of
msgid "Raised when an operation would make the graph invalid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Result:1 of
msgid ""
"Signals computed by :meth:`Graph.run`, by port reference or "
"``\"id.port\"`` string."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Result:3 of
msgid ""
"The :class:`~lumos.results.RunArchive` written by ``ctx.run(..., "
"archive=...)``, or ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Result:4 of
msgid ""
"In operation with the digital twin, the simulated outputs of the "
"measuring elements (the result itself holds the measurements)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Result:6 of
msgid "Measured minus simulated outputs, where both are comparable data products."
