#: lumos.core.group:1 of
msgid ""
"Element groups: composite elements exposing some of their internal ports "
"(REQ-CTX-7)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.group:3 of
msgid ""
"An :class:`ElementGroup` holds a sub-graph of elements (a planetary "
"system, a photonic chip and its components, a multi-lens objective...) "
"and **exposes** chosen internal ports as its own ports. It is an "
":class:`~lumos.core.element.Element`: it can be added to a context or to "
"another group, connected with ``>>`` and saved to ``.lumos`` (``kind: "
"\"group\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.group:16 of
msgid ""
"When the group runs, the signals arriving on its exposed inputs are fed "
"to the internal ports and the internal graph computes the exposed outputs"
" with its own cache. A change of a parameter of any child invalidates the"
" results of the group, and therefore everything downstream of it, in the "
"enclosing graph."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.group.ElementGroup:1 of
