#: lumos.core.action:1 of
msgid "Timed actions of elements (REQ-EL-5, REQ-EL-6)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.action:3 of
msgid ""
"An action is a method of an element that changes the state of the "
"equipment it represents: move a stage, open a shutter, take an exposure. "
"It is declared with the :func:`action` decorator and a duration, fixed or"
" computed from the element properties before the action runs::"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.action:15 of
msgid ""
"When the element belongs to a context, calling the action goes through "
"the context: in simulation the body updates the virtual state, the "
"command is logged and the clock advances by the duration; in operation "
"the command is sent to the driver (see :mod:`lumos.core.driver`). Outside"
" a context the body simply runs."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.action.ActionSpec:1 of
msgid ""
"Description of an action: its name, its duration and the undecorated "
"method."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.action.ActionSpec.duration_si:1 of
msgid "Duration of a call, in seconds (computed before the action runs)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.action.action:1 of
msgid "Declare a method as a timed action."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.action.action:3 of
msgid ""
"A time quantity, a function ``(self, *args, **kwargs) -> quantity`` "
"evaluated before the action, or ``None`` for an instantaneous action."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:1 of
msgid "Drivers of real or emulated equipment (REQ-HW-1)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`Driver` connects an element to the equipment it represents. In "
"operation mode, the actions of the element become :class:`Command` "
"objects sent to the driver, which answers with a :class:`Reply`: the "
"measured duration, the state read back from the equipment and an optional"
" value. Concrete drivers implement the protected methods ``_connect``, "
"``_disconnect``, ``_send``, ``_query`` and ``_stop`` on top of a "
"transport (serial, TCP, VISA, vendor SDK; phase 12)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:9 of
msgid ""
":class:`SimulatedDriver` sends nothing: it records the commands and "
"answers with the virtual state of its element, which makes it possible to"
" test a sequence of commands without any equipment."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:13 of
msgid "Safety (REQ-HW-4, ADR-0014)"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:14 of
msgid ""
"Every driver inherits these checks, applied in :meth:`Driver.send` to "
"every command, whether it comes from an element action or is sent "
"directly:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:17 of
msgid ""
"**limits**: ``limits`` maps ``\"action.argument\"`` to ``(low, high)`` "
"quantities; ``signatures`` gives the names of the positional arguments of"
" each action. A value outside its range raises :class:`LimitError`;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:19 of
msgid ""
"**dry run**: with ``dry_run=True`` the command is checked and logged (as "
"a warning), never sent;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:20 of
msgid ""
"**confirmations**: the actions listed in ``dangerous`` are sent only if "
"the ``confirm`` callback accepts the command (:class:`ActionRefused` "
"otherwise, also when no callback is set);"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:22 of
msgid ""
"**recovery**: a :class:`ConnectionLost` from the equipment triggers a "
"reconnection and a new attempt, at most ``retries`` times; "
":class:`DriverTimeout` reports an equipment that does not answer;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:24 of
msgid ""
"**emergency stop**: :meth:`Driver.stop` may be called from another "
"thread; it interrupts the waits of a command in progress "
"(:meth:`Driver.wait`), which then raises :class:`DriverStopped`. The "
"driver refuses new commands until :meth:`Driver.reset`;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:27 of
msgid ""
"**safe state**: :meth:`Driver.safe_state` brings the equipment to a safe "
"state (laser off, shutter closed...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.driver:30 of
msgid ""
"States: ``\"disconnected\"``, ``\"ready\"``, ``\"busy\"`` (a command in "
"progress), ``\"stopped\"`` (after an emergency stop) and ``\"error\"`` "
"(after a failure)."
msgstr ""

