":func:`kernel_nuller`, ``(..., 3)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.elements.detectors:1 of
msgid "Detectors (§5.9, step P6.9): camera, photodiode and power meter."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.elements.detectors:3 of
msgid ""
"Detectors turn light into :class:`~lumos.fields.DataProduct` "
"measurements. Every spectral channel :math:`k` of weight :math:`w_k` "
"(spectral quadrature weights of wavecubes) is converted to a photon rate "
":math:`N_k = P_k \\lambda_k / (hc)` when its power is in watts; "
"incoherent modes add with their weights."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.elements.detectors:8 of
msgid "Camera"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.elements.detectors:9 of
msgid ""
"The pixels are the samples of the incoming field (propagate it to the "
"detector grid first, e.g. with :class:`~lumos.elements.optics.FreeSpace` "
"and an ``output_grid``). During an exposure :math:`t`, a pixel collects "
"on average :math:`\\bar n = t\\,(\\sum_k w_k \\eta(\\lambda_k) N_k + D)` "
"electrons (quantum efficiency :math:`\\eta`, dark current :math:`D`). "
"With ``noise=True`` the charge is a Poisson draw, clipped at the full "
"well, summed over ``binning`` × ``binning`` pixels (charge binning), read"
" once with a Gaussian read noise, converted with the gain :math:`g` "
"(e⁻/ADU), offset by the bias, rounded and clipped to the range of the "
"``bits``-bit converter (Janesick, *Photon Transfer*, 2007). With "
"``noise=False`` the camera returns the expected value, clipped the same "
"way but not rounded. :meth:`Camera.expose` is a timed action lasting the "
"exposure time; each exposure draws a new frame from the reproducible "
"random stream of the camera."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.elements.detectors:20 of
msgid "Photodiode and power meter"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.elements.detectors:21 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A photodiode delivers the current :math:`I = q \\sum_k w_k \\eta N_k + "
"I_\\mathrm{dark}` (responsivity :math:`\\eta q \\lambda / hc`) with the "
"shot noise :math:`\\sigma_I = \\sqrt{2 q I \\Delta f}` over its bandwidth"
" (Schottky 1918); :meth:`Photodiode.acquire` takes a new sample. A power "
"meter reads the power in watts. Both read a beam or a guided lane (all "
"its modes) as one value, and a :class:`~lumos.fields.Bus` as one value "
"per lane (axis ``channel``, ADR-0023)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.elements.detectors.Camera:1 of
msgid ""
"Pixel detector: quantum efficiency, photon, dark and read noises, gain, "
"saturation and binning."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.elements.detectors.Camera.twin_feed:1 of
