msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.diffuse.UniformDisk:1 of
msgid ""
"Disk of uniform surface brightness (resolved star, planet, uniform "
"nebula)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.diffuse.ZodiacalLight:1 of
msgid ""
"Local zodiacal light: uniform, with scattered sunlight and thermal dust "
"emission."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.diffuse.sersic_b:1 of
msgid ""
"Return :math:`b_n`, solution of :math:`P(2n, b_n) = 1/2` (half of the "
"light within :math:`R_e`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:1 of
msgid ""
"Mapped scene components: radiance maps from files and arrays (step P8.4, "
"REQ-SCN-4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`MappedComponent` holds a surface-brightness map "
":math:`\\Sigma_\\nu` (stored in Jy sr⁻¹) on a rectangular angular grid, "
"either one image with a spectral shape or a spectral cube, and produces "
"the spectral radiance :math:`L_\\lambda = \\Sigma_\\nu\\,c/\\lambda^2` at"
" the channels of the context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:8 of
msgid "Sources"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:9 of
msgid ""
":meth:`MappedComponent.from_fits`: FITS images and cubes with a celestial"
" WCS (Calabretta & Greisen 2002, A&A 395, 1077). Pixel scales come from "
"the WCS; the brightness unit from ``BUNIT`` or the ``unit`` argument. "
"Images are oriented with East towards +x and North towards +y, as "
"everywhere in LUMOS: an image whose right ascension decreases with the "
"column index (``CDELT1 < 0``, the usual orientation) is flipped left-"
"right. A third, spectral axis (``WAVE``, ``FREQ``...) gives the "
"wavelengths of the planes of a cube."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:14 of
msgid ":meth:`MappedComponent.from_array`: a quantity array and pixel scales."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:15 of
msgid ""
":meth:`MappedComponent.from_image`: PNG, JPEG or TIFF images (read by "
"matplotlib) with a calibration, the surface brightness of a pixel value "
"of 1; colour images are averaged over their RGB channels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:19 of
msgid "Brightness units"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:20 of
msgid ""
"Accepted brightness units: per solid angle (``Jy/sr``, ``MJy/sr``, "
"``Jy/arcsec2``, ``W m-2 sr-1 m-1``, ``erg s-1 cm-2 Å-1 arcsec-2``...) or "
"per pixel (``Jy``, ``Jy/pixel``, ``W m-2 m-1``...), divided by the pixel "
"solid angle. Quantities per unit wavelength are converted to per unit "
"frequency with :math:`F_\\nu = F_\\lambda\\,\\lambda^2 / c` at the "
"wavelength of each plane (images: ``reference_wavelength``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:26 of
msgid "Spectra"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:27 of
msgid ""
"An image is scaled to other wavelengths with a flat :math:`F_\\nu` or a "
"blackbody shape, as the parametric components "
"(:mod:`lumos.scenes.diffuse`). The planes of a cube are interpolated "
"linearly in wavelength; outside the range of the cube the nearest plane "
"is used and a warning is logged."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped:31 of
msgid ""
"The flux of the map is conserved when a :class:`~lumos.scenes.Scene` "
"resamples it onto its grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent:1 of
msgid "Surface-brightness map (image or spectral cube) on an angular grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.transfer:1 of
msgid "Return the spectral radiance of the map at the channels of the context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.from_array:1 of
msgid ""
"Create a component from a map ``(ny, nx)`` or a cube ``(nλ, ny, nx)`` "
"with its brightness unit."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.from_array:3 of
msgid ""
"Rows go from South to North and columns from West to East (x points East,"
" y North)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.from_fits:1 of
msgid ""
"Create a component from a FITS image or cube with a celestial WCS (see "
"the module notes)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.from_hdu:1 of
msgid "Create a component from a FITS HDU (image or cube) with a celestial WCS."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.from_survey:1 of
msgid ""
"Create a component from a survey image of ``target`` (SkyView, see "
":mod:`lumos.catalogs.surveys`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.from_survey:3 of
msgid ""
"Survey images are rarely calibrated: give the brightness of one data unit"
" (``calibration``) or the total flux density of the image "
"(``flux_density``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.from_image:1 of
msgid ""
"Create a component from a PNG, JPEG or TIFF image; ``calibration`` is the"
" brightness of a value 1."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.MappedComponent.from_image:3 of
msgid ""
"The first row of the file is the top of the image (North); colour images "
"are averaged over RGB."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.to_surface_brightness:1 of
msgid "Convert a map to a surface brightness per unit frequency (Jy sr⁻¹)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.to_surface_brightness:3 of
msgid ""
"Map in a unit per solid angle, per pixel (``Jy/pixel``) or of flux per "
"pixel (``Jy``), per unit frequency or wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.to_surface_brightness:5 of
msgid "Solid angle of a pixel."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.to_surface_brightness:6 of
msgid ""
"Wavelength(s) at which per-wavelength quantities are converted, "
"broadcastable against ``values``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.mapped.to_surface_brightness:8 of
msgid "If the unit is not a spectral brightness or flux."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:1 of
msgid ""
"Procedural scene components: random fields and test targets (step P8.6, "
"REQ-SCN-8, §5.9)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each component draws a pattern :math:`P \\in [0, 1]` (relative level) on "
"its own grid and produces the spectral radiance :math:`L_\\lambda = "
"\\Sigma_\\nu(\\lambda)\\,P\\,c/\\lambda^2`, with the surface brightness "
"``surface_brightness`` :math:`\\Sigma_{\\nu,0}` at "
"``reference_wavelength`` and a flat or blackbody spectral shape, as the "
"backgrounds of :mod:`lumos.scenes.diffuse`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:9 of
msgid "Grids"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:10 of
msgid ""
"The grid has ``n_pixels`` × ``n_pixels`` pixels. By default it is "
"angular, with pixels of ``pixel_scale`` (sky scenes); with ``pixel_size``"
" > 0 it is spatial, with pixels of that length (laboratory scenes, at the"
" distance of the :class:`~lumos.scenes.Scene`). The **sizes of the "
"patterns** (radius, period, length) are angles on angular grids, lengths "
"on spatial grids, or numbers of pixels (``u.pix`` or a plain number) on "
"both, so that the same target serves both kinds of scene; a size "
":math:`s` covers :math:`s/p` pixels of size :math:`p`. Positions are "
"measured from the central pixel ``N // 2`` (§9 of the specifications). "
"Edges are anti-aliased by averaging ``supersample`` × ``supersample`` "
"sub-pixels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:19 of
msgid "Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:20 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":class:`GaussianRandomField`: a log-normal random texture of mean "
"``surface_brightness``, relative standard deviation ``contrast`` and "
"power spectrum :math:`\\propto k^{-\\beta}` (``spectral_index`` β). White"
" Gaussian noise is filtered by :math:`k^{-\\beta/2}` in Fourier space, "
"standardised to :math:`z`, then :math:`P \\propto \\exp(s z)` with "
":math:`s^2 = \\ln(1 + c^2)` (log-normal of coefficient of variation "
":math:`c`), and finally rescaled to the exact mean and contrast. For "
"small contrasts the power spectrum keeps the slope :math:`-\\beta` "
"(Wiener-Khinchin theorem). The noise comes from the reproducible random "
"stream of the element (ADR-0007)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:27 of
msgid ""
":class:`SiemensStar`: ``n_spokes`` bright sectors alternating with dark "
"ones within ``radius``; the local period grows with the radius, which "
"probes all spatial frequencies (ISO 12233)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:29 of
msgid ""
":class:`Checkerboard`: squares of side ``period / 2`` with a corner on "
"the axis."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural:30 of
msgid ""
":class:`BarTarget`: ``n_bars`` vertical bars of width ``period / 2`` and "
"length ``length``, centred, as in one element of the USAF 1951 resolution"
" chart (MIL-STD-150A)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.BarTarget:1 of
msgid "Group of bright vertical bars (one element of a USAF 1951 chart)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural._anti_aliased.<locals>.transfer:1 of
msgid "Return the radiance of the pattern on its grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.Checkerboard:1 of
msgid "Checkerboard of squares of side ``period / 2``, a corner on the axis."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.GaussianRandomField:1 of
msgid "Log-normal random texture with a power-law power spectrum."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.GaussianRandomField.transfer:1 of
msgid "Return a reproducible random texture."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.ProceduralComponent:1 of
msgid ""
"Base class of procedural components: brightness, spectrum and grid "
"(angular or spatial)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.SiemensStar:1 of
msgid "Siemens star: alternating bright and dark sectors."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.TargetSize:1 of
msgid ""
"Size of a test target: an angle, a length, pixels (``u.pix``) or a plain "
"number of pixels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.TargetSize.validate:1 of
msgid ""
"Accept a positive number (pixels) or a scalar quantity of pixels, angle "
"or length."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.TargetSize.encode:1 of
msgid "Return the JSON form: a number of pixels or a quantity."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.procedural.TargetSize.decode:1 of
msgid "Return the size of a JSON form."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:1 of
msgid "Imaging of extended incoherent scenes (step P8.5, REQ-SCN-6, ADR-0011)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:3 of
msgid ""
"An extended scene is a radiance map :math:`L(\\theta, \\lambda)` "
"(:class:`~lumos.fields.RadianceField`). Its points are mutually "
"incoherent, so the image is the sum of the images of its points, weighted"
" by their flux (Goodman, *Introduction to Fourier Optics*, §6.1). "
":func:`image_scene` computes it through an :class:`ImagingSystem`, a part"
" of a context going from an input that receives point sources "
"(:class:`~lumos.fields.SourceList`, e.g. ``\"telescope.in\"``) to an "
"output field (e.g. ``\"camera_plane.out\"``), with one of three "
"strategies:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:10 of
msgid "``\"isoplanatic\"``"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:11 of
msgid ""
"The point-spread function (PSF) does not depend on the position in the "
"field: the image is the convolution of the scene by the on-axis PSF "
":math:`h`, computed with FFTs channel by channel,"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:14 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"I(\\mathbf{x}) = \\sum_j F_j\\, h(\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{p}\\,\\theta_j),"
"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:16 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"with :math:`F_j = L(\\theta_j)\\,\\Delta\\Omega` the flux of scene pixel "
":math:`j` and :math:`\\mathbf{p}` the plate scale (focal-plane position "
"per unit angle), measured on the system from the images of two off-axis "
"points. The scene is first resampled, conserving its flux, onto an "
"angular grid whose pixels map exactly onto the detector pixels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:20 of
msgid "``\"anisoplanatic\"``"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:21 of
msgid ""
"The PSF varies slowly across the field: PSFs :math:`h_k` are computed on "
"a grid of field points :math:`\\theta_k` and interpolated with bilinear "
"weights :math:`w_k(\\theta)`, :math:`I = \\sum_k (w_k F) * h_k` (weighted"
" convolutions; Lauer 2002, Proc. SPIE 4847, 167)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:24 of
msgid "``\"decomposition\"``"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:25 of
msgid ""
"Every scene pixel becomes a point source and the whole system is computed"
" for all of them at once (an :class:`~lumos.fields.IncoherentBundle` mode"
" per pixel). It is exact for any system and compulsory for systems that "
"are not shift-invariant: coronagraphs, interferometers, fibre injection."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.scenes.imaging:29 of
msgid ""
"``strategy=\"auto\"`` probes the system: it compares the image of an off-"
"axis point, shifted back by the plate scale, with the on-axis PSF. When "
"they agree within 1 % (L1 norm) the system is shift-invariant and the "
"convolution is used; otherwise the scene is decomposed. Forcing "
