#: lumos.physics.radiometry:1 of
msgid ""
"Radiometry: radiance, irradiance, étendue and photon counting (step P8.2,"
" REQ-SCN-5)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry:3 of
msgid ""
"Definitions (McCluney, *Introduction to Radiometry and Photometry*, 2nd "
"ed., ch. 2):"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry:5 of
msgid ""
"the **radiance** :math:`L` is the power per unit projected area and per "
"unit solid angle (W m⁻² sr⁻¹; *spectral* radiance :math:`L_\\lambda` per "
"unit wavelength, W m⁻² sr⁻¹ m⁻¹). It is invariant along a ray in a "
"lossless medium;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry:8 of
msgid ""
"a pupil of area :math:`A` receiving the radiance :math:`L` from a solid "
"angle :math:`\\Omega` small enough for the obliquity to be negligible "
"collects the power :math:`P = L\\,A\\,\\Omega`; the product :math:`G = "
"A\\,\\Omega` is the **étendue**, which for a cone of half-angle "
":math:`\\alpha` filled by a Lambertian source is :math:`G = \\pi A "
"\\sin^2\\alpha` (Welford & Winston, *High Collection Nonimaging Optics*, "
"§2.6);"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry:13 of
msgid ""
"a Lambertian surface of radiance :math:`L` has the exitance :math:`M = "
"\\pi L`; a uniform disk of radiance :math:`L` subtending the angular "
"radius :math:`\\theta` produces the irradiance :math:`E = \\pi L "
"\\sin^2\\theta` on a surface facing it;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry:16 of
msgid ""
"the solid angle of a cone of half-angle :math:`\\alpha` is :math:`2\\pi(1"
" - \\cos\\alpha)`;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry:17 of
msgid ""
"a photon of wavelength :math:`\\lambda` carries the energy "
":math:`hc/\\lambda`: spectral quantities in watts become photon rates by "
"multiplying by :math:`\\lambda / hc` at each wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry:20 of
msgid ""
"The blackbody spectral radiance is Planck's law "
"(:mod:`lumos.physics.blackbody`); magnitudes and bands are in "
":mod:`lumos.physics.photometry`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.blackbody_radiance:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the spectral radiance :math:`B_\\lambda(T)` of a blackbody (W m⁻² "
"sr⁻¹ m⁻¹), Planck's law."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.cone_solid_angle:1 of
msgid ""
"Solid angle :math:`2\\pi(1 - \\cos\\alpha)` of a cone of half-angle "
":math:`\\alpha`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.disk_irradiance:1 of
msgid ""
"Irradiance :math:`\\pi L \\sin^2\\theta` of a uniform disk of angular "
"radius θ, facing the surface."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.etendue:1 of
msgid ""
"Étendue :math:`\\pi A \\sin^2\\alpha` of an area receiving a Lambertian "
"cone of half-angle α."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.flux_from_ab_magnitude:1 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Spectral flux density :math:`F_\\nu = 3631\\ \\mathrm{Jy} \\times "
"10^{-0.4 m}` of an AB magnitude."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.integrate_spectrum:1 of
msgid ""
"Integrate a spectral quantity over wavelength with the trapezoidal rule "
"(last axis)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.lambertian_exitance:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the exitance :math:`M = \\pi L` of a Lambertian surface (any "
"radiance unit, spectral or not)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.photon_energy:1 of
msgid ""
"Energy :math:`hc/\\lambda` of a photon of vacuum wavelength "
"``wavelength``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.pupil_power:1 of
msgid ""
"Power :math:`L\\,A\\,\\Omega` collected by a pupil of area ``A`` from a "
"small solid angle Ω."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.to_energy:1 of
msgid ""
"Convert a photon-based quantity (photon s⁻¹, photon s⁻¹ m⁻²...) to the "
"energy-based one (W...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.to_photons:1 of
msgid ""
"Convert an energy-based quantity (W, W m⁻² sr⁻¹ m⁻¹...) to the photon-"
"based one at ``wavelength``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.physics.radiometry.to_photons:3 of
msgid ""
"The power unit W is replaced by photon s⁻¹; any other factor of the unit "
"is kept."
msgstr ""

