msgid ""
"VizieR photometry: the spectral energy distribution gathered by the CDS "
"SED service."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.vizier:3 of
msgid ""
"The VizieR photometry viewer (Allen et al. 2014, ASPC 485, 193) collects,"
" around a position or a name, every photometric point of the VizieR "
"catalogues: frequency, flux density, uncertainty, filter and catalogue. "
"They are returned as a :class:`PhotometricPoints` table, the raw material"
" of the SED fusion (:mod:`lumos.catalogs.sed`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.vizier.PhotometricPoints:1 of
msgid "Photometric measurements of one object."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.vizier.PhotometricPoints:3 of
msgid "Effective wavelengths of the filters."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.vizier.PhotometricPoints:5 of
msgid "Spectral flux densities per unit frequency (Jy)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.SpectralEnergyDistribution:7
#: lumos.catalogs.vizier.PhotometricPoints:7 of
msgid "Uncertainties (NaN when unknown)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.vizier.PhotometricPoints:9 of
msgid "Names of the filters (``\"Johnson:V\"``, ``\"2MASS:Ks\"``...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.vizier.PhotometricPoints:11 of
msgid "VizieR tables of the measurements (``\"II/246/out\"``...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.vizier.VizierPhotometry:1 of
msgid ""
"VizieR (CDS) photometry viewer: every photometric point of the VizieR "
"catalogues."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.vizier.VizierPhotometry.sed:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the photometric points within ``radius`` of ``target`` (a name or "
"\"ra dec\" in degrees)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:1 of
msgid ""
"Fusion and completion of spectral energy distributions (step P9.7, REQ-"
"CAT-4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:4 of
msgid "Fusion rules"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:5 of
msgid ""
":func:`fuse` turns photometric points from many catalogues "
"(:class:`~lumos.catalogs.vizier.PhotometricPoints`) into one "
":class:`SpectralEnergyDistribution`, one point per filter:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:8 of
msgid "points without a positive, finite flux density are dropped;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:9 of
msgid "points are grouped by filter name;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:10 of
msgid ""
"within a filter, the points of the highest-priority catalogue present are"
" kept (``priorities``, VizieR table prefixes, :data:`DEFAULT_PRIORITIES` "
"by default);"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:12 of
msgid "among them, the point with the smallest relative uncertainty is chosen;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:13 of
msgid "when none has an uncertainty, the median of their flux densities is used."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:15 of
msgid "The result is sorted by wavelength and keeps the catalogue of each point."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:18 of
msgid "Completion"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed:19 of
msgid ""
":func:`fit_blackbody` fits :math:`F_\\nu = \\Omega\\,B_\\nu(T)` to the "
"SED (least squares on :math:`\\log F_\\nu`): temperature :math:`T` and "
"solid angle :math:`\\Omega = \\pi (\\theta/2)^2` of the photosphere of "
"angular diameter :math:`\\theta`. "
":meth:`SpectralEnergyDistribution.complete` adds points of the fitted "
"blackbody where the SED has none, and :func:`complete_star` fills the "
"missing temperature, distance (:math:`1/\\varpi`) and radius (:math:`R = "
"\\theta d / 2`) of a star record. Completed values are **flagged as "
"estimated** (``source=\"lumos\"``); measured values are never replaced."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.DEFAULT_PRIORITIES:1 of
msgid "homogeneous all-sky surveys first."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.DEFAULT_PRIORITIES:3 of
msgid "Default priority of catalogues (VizieR prefixes)"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.SpectralEnergyDistribution:1 of
msgid "Fused SED: one flux density per filter."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.SpectralEnergyDistribution:3 of
msgid "Effective wavelengths, increasing."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.SpectralEnergyDistribution:5 of
msgid "Flux densities per unit frequency (Jy)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.SpectralEnergyDistribution:9 of
msgid "Filter names."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.SpectralEnergyDistribution:11 of
msgid "Catalogue of each point (``\"lumos\"`` for estimated points)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.SpectralEnergyDistribution:13 of
msgid "Whether each point was estimated by a completion."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.SpectralEnergyDistribution.complete:1 of
msgid ""
"Return a copy with the fitted blackbody added at ``wavelengths`` (points "
"flagged estimated)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.complete_star:1 of
msgid ""
"Return a copy of ``record`` with the missing temperature, distance and "
"radius estimated from ``sed``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.complete_star:3 of
msgid ""
"A measured temperature is kept and used to fit the solid angle; otherwise"
" both are fitted."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.fit_blackbody:1 of
msgid ""
"Fit a blackbody to the measured points of ``sed``: return its temperature"
" and solid angle."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.fit_blackbody:3 of
msgid ""
"With ``temperature`` given, only the solid angle is fitted (mean of the "
"logarithmic residuals)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.sed.fuse:1 of
msgid ""
"Fuse photometric points into one point per filter (see the module "
"documentation for the rules)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.calspec:1 of
msgid ""
"CALSPEC: the flux standards of the Hubble Space Telescope (Bohlin, Gordon"
" & Tremblay 2014, PASP 126, 711)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.calspec:3 of
msgid ""
"The spectra are FITS tables (``WAVELENGTH`` in Å, ``FLUX`` in erg s⁻¹ "
"cm⁻² Å⁻¹) in the ``current_calspec`` directory of STScI. "
":meth:`Calspec.spectrum` finds the latest file of a star, preferring the "
"measured STIS spectrum (``<star>_stis_NNN.fits``) to a model "
"(``<star>_mod_NNN.fits``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.calspec.Calspec:1 of
msgid "CALSPEC spectrophotometric standards (STScI)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.calspec.Calspec.files:1 of
msgid "Return the names of the FITS files of the directory."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.calspec.Calspec.file_of:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the latest file of ``star`` (a CALSPEC root name such as "
"``\"alpha_lyr\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.calspec.Calspec.spectrum:1 of
msgid "Return the spectrum of ``star`` (F_λ in erg s⁻¹ cm⁻² Å⁻¹)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.models:1 of
msgid "Libraries of model and empirical spectra (step P9.5)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.models:3 of
msgid ""
":class:`PicklesLibrary` reads the stellar spectral flux library of "
"Pickles (1998, PASP 110, 863), 131 spectral types from O5 to M10 (dwarfs "
"to supergiants), 1150 Å to 2.5 µm (``UVKLIB``), from the copy of the "
"STScI reference atlases (``grid/pickles/dat_uvk``). The index "
"``pickles_uk.fits`` maps spectral types to files."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.models.PicklesLibrary:1 of
msgid "Pickles (1998) library of stellar spectra (STScI reference atlases)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.models.PicklesLibrary.index:1 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Return the file of each spectral type (``{\"A0V\": \"pickles_uk_9\", "
"...}``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.models.PicklesLibrary.file_of:1 of
msgid "Return the file name (without extension) of ``spectral_type``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.models.PicklesLibrary.spectrum:1 of
msgid "Return the spectrum of ``spectral_type`` (F_λ, arbitrary normalisation)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.svo:1 of
msgid ""
"SVO Filter Profile Service (Rodrigo & Solano 2020, Spanish Virtual "
"Observatory)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.svo:3 of
msgid ""
":meth:`SvoFilterService.filter` returns the transmission curve of a "
"filter identified as ``<facility>/<instrument>.<band>`` "
"(``\"Generic/Johnson.V\"``, ``\"2MASS/2MASS.Ks\"``, "
"``\"JWST/NIRCam.F444W\"``...), with the zero point of its photometric "
"system when the service gives one."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.svo.SvoFilterService:1 of
msgid "Transmission curves of photometric filters (SVO Filter Profile Service)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.svo.SvoFilterService.filter:1 of
msgid "Return the transmission curve of the filter ``identifier``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.solar_system:1 of
msgid ""
"Solar System: JPL Horizons ephemerides and the reference solar spectrum "
"(step P9.4, REQ-CAT-2)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.solar_system:3 of
msgid ""
":class:`Horizons` queries the JPL Horizons API (Giorgini et al. 1996, "
"BAAS 28, 1158) for observer tables: apparent position (ICRF), apparent "
"diameter, heliocentric distance ``r``, distance to the observer ``Δ`` and"
" phase angle (Sun-Target-Observer), one "
":class:`~lumos.catalogs.records.SolarSystemRecord` per epoch."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.solar_system:6 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
":func:`solar_spectrum` returns the solar reference spectrum at 1 au of "
"CALSPEC (``sun_reference_stis``, Bohlin, Dickinson & Calzetti 2001, AJ "
"122, 2118): HST/STIS and ground measurements from 0.12 to 0.96 µm "
"extended by a Kurucz model to 2.7 µm. Its integral (1326 W m⁻²) is the "
"total solar irradiance minus the 2.5 % emitted beyond 2.7 µm."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.solar_system.BODIES:1 of
msgid "Horizons identifiers of the major bodies."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.solar_system.Horizons:1 of
msgid "JPL Horizons ephemerides of Solar-System bodies."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.solar_system.Horizons.command:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the Horizons command of ``body``: the identifier of a major body, "
"else ``body`` itself."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.solar_system.Horizons.ephemeris:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the apparent positions and distances of ``body`` seen from "
"``observer`` (geocentre)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.solar_system.solar_spectrum:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the CALSPEC solar reference spectrum at 1 au (F_λ in erg s⁻¹ cm⁻² "
"Å⁻¹)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.archives:1 of
msgid ""
"Observation archives (ESO, MAST) and infrared catalogues (IRSA), through "
"their TAP services."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.archives:3 of
msgid ""
":class:`Eso` and :class:`Mast` list the observations of a target in the "
"IVOA ObsCore model (instrument, product type, position, spectral "
"coverage, date, access URL): ESO Science Archive and the Mikulski Archive"
" for Space Telescopes (HST, JWST, TESS...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.archives:6 of
msgid ""
":class:`Irsa` reads the 2MASS point-source catalogue (Skrutskie et al. "
"2006, AJ 131, 1163) at IPAC/IRSA."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.archives.Eso:1 of
msgid "ESO Science Archive (ObsCore)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.archives.Irsa:1 of
msgid "NASA/IPAC Infrared Science Archive: 2MASS point sources."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.archives.Irsa.two_mass:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the J, H and Ks magnitudes of the nearest 2MASS source within "
"``radius``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.archives.Mast:1 of
msgid "Mikulski Archive for Space Telescopes (ObsCore of the CAOM database)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys:1 of
msgid "Images of diffuse objects from sky surveys (step P9.6, REQ-CAT-3)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys:3 of
msgid ""
":class:`SkyView` (NASA GSFC, McGlynn, Scollick & White 1998) resamples "
"dozens of surveys (DSS, 2MASS, WISE, GALEX...) around a name or a "
"position."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys:5 of
msgid ""
":class:`Hips2Fits` (CDS, Fernique et al. 2015, A&A 578, A114) cuts FITS "
"images out of any HiPS survey (``CDS/P/DSS2/red``, ``CDS/P/2MASS/K``...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys:8 of
msgid ""
":func:`survey_component` turns an image into a "
":class:`~lumos.scenes.MappedComponent`. Survey images are rarely "
"calibrated in brightness: the brightness of one data unit "
"(``calibration``) or the total flux density of the image "
"(``flux_density``) must be given when the header has no ``BUNIT``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.Hips2Fits:1 of
msgid "hips2fits (CDS): FITS cut-outs of HiPS surveys."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.Hips2Fits.image:1 of
msgid ""
"Return a square FITS cut-out of ``hips`` centred on ``(ra, dec)``, of "
"field of view ``fov``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.SkyView:1 of
msgid ""
"SkyView virtual observatory (NASA GSFC): survey images resampled around a"
" target."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.SkyView.image:1 of
msgid ""
"Return a FITS image (``astropy.io.fits.PrimaryHDU``) of ``target`` in "
"``survey``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.survey_component:1 of
msgid "Turn a survey image into a :class:`~lumos.scenes.MappedComponent`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.survey_component:3 of
msgid "FITS image with a celestial WCS."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.survey_component:4 of
msgid "Name of the component."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.survey_component:5 of
msgid ""
"Brightness of one data unit (e.g. ``1e-3 * u.MJy / u.sr``), for images "
"without ``BUNIT``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.catalogs.surveys.survey_component:6 of
msgid ""
"Total flux density of the image: the data are scaled so that their sum is"
