#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:3 of
msgid ""
"Symbolic fields of known families carry a **form** "
"(:attr:`~lumos.symbolic.SymbolicField.form`) that elements update "
"exactly:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:6 of
msgid "Gaussian beams (:class:`GaussianBeamForm`)"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:7 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Hermite-Gauss :math:`\\mathrm{HG}_{nm}` and Laguerre-Gauss "
":math:`\\mathrm{LG}_{p\\ell}` modes are described by the complex beam "
"parameter :math:`q`, with :math:`1/q = 1/R + i\\lambda/(\\pi w^2)` in the"
" :math:`e^{+ikz}` convention of LUMOS (a beam at a distance :math:`z` "
"after its waist has :math:`q = z - i z_R`). Through an ABCD system "
":math:`q \\to (Aq + B)/(Cq + D)`, and the field gains the Gouy phase "
":math:`\\arg(A + B/q)` per unit of mode order :math:`N + 1` (:math:`N = n"
" + m` or :math:`2p + |\\ell|`) (Kogelnik & Li 1966, Appl. Opt. 5, 1550; "
"Siegman, *Lasers*, ch. 20). Free space of length :math:`d` is :math:`(1, "
"d, 0, 1)` and adds the phase :math:`kd`; a thin lens is :math:`(1, 0, "
"-1/f, 1)`. The fields are"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:16 of
msgid ""
"U_{nm} = \\sqrt{P}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{\\pi}}\\frac{1}{w\\sqrt{2^{n+m} "
"n!\\,m!}}\n"
"         H_n\\!\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2 x}{w}\\right) "
"H_m\\!\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2 y}{w}\\right)\n"
"         e^{ik r^2/2q}\\,e^{-i(n+m+1)\\psi}\\,e^{i\\phi},\n"
"\n"
"U_{p\\ell} = \\sqrt{P}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\,p!}{\\pi "
"(p+|\\ell|)!}}\\frac{1}{w}\n"
"            \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt2 r}{w}\\right)^{|\\ell|} "
"L_p^{|\\ell|}\\!\\left(\\frac{2r^2}{w^2}\\right)\n"
"            e^{i\\ell\\varphi}\\,e^{ik "
"r^2/2q}\\,e^{-i(2p+|\\ell|+1)\\psi}\\,e^{i\\phi},"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:25 of
msgid ""
"normalised to the power :math:`P` (:math:`\\psi` accumulated Gouy phase, "
":math:`\\phi` accumulated phase :math:`kd`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:28 of
msgid "Uniform pupils (:class:`PupilForm`)"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:29 of
msgid ""
"A plane wave of amplitude :math:`A` through a circular or rectangular "
"aperture, then a thin lens of focal length :math:`f`, gives in the focal "
"plane (:math:`d = f`) the Fraunhofer pattern of the pupil (Goodman, "
"*Introduction to Fourier Optics*, §5.2): :math:`U = "
"\\frac{e^{ikf}}{i\\lambda f} e^{ikr^2/2f}\\, \\tilde "
"P\\!\\left(\\frac{x}{\\lambda f}, \\frac{y}{\\lambda f}\\right)` with "
":math:`\\tilde P = A\\,\\frac{\\pi D^2}{4}\\,\\frac{2J_1(v)}{v}`, "
":math:`v = \\pi D r/(\\lambda f)` (circle) or "
":math:`A\\,ab\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(ax/\\lambda "
"f)\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(by/\\lambda f)` (rectangle)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:37 of
msgid "Fallback"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.symbolic.closed_forms:38 of
msgid ""
"Any other propagation samples the field on its grid hint "
"(:attr:`SymbolicField.grid`), propagates it numerically "
"(:func:`lumos.propagation.propagate`) and returns a "
":class:`~lumos.fields.Wavefront`; the journal records it."
msgstr ""

