#: lumos.hardware.protocol.format_identity:1 of
msgid "Return ``VENDOR,MODEL,SERIAL,FIRMWARE``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.protocol.format_reply:1 of
msgid "Return an ``OK`` reply with its values."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.protocol.format_token:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the token of a value: quantity ``12.5[mm]``, number, boolean "
"(``1``/``0``) or word."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.protocol.parse_command:1 of
msgid "Return the verb (upper case) and the arguments of a command line."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.protocol.parse_identity:1 of
msgid "Parse ``VENDOR,MODEL,SERIAL,FIRMWARE``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.protocol.parse_reply:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the values of an ``OK`` reply; raise the exception of an ``ERR`` "
"reply."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.protocol.parse_token:1 of
msgid "Return the value of a token (quantity, int, float or word)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery:1 of
msgid ""
"Discovery of equipment and association with the elements of a context "
"(step P12.6, REQ-HW-2)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery:3 of
msgid ""
":func:`discover` opens each candidate connection (TCP addresses, serial "
"ports, VISA resources), asks ``*IDN?`` and keeps the devices that "
"identify themselves as ``VENDOR,MODEL,SERIAL,FIRMWARE``; connections that"
" fail or answer something else are skipped. :func:`associate` attaches to"
" every element declaring a ``lumoslabs_model`` (or ``device_model``) the "
"driver of a discovered device of that model, and connects it. When "
"several devices or elements share a model, ``assignments`` maps element "
"paths to serial numbers."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.DeviceInfo:1 of
msgid "A discovered device: identity and URL of its connection."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.associate:1 of
msgid ""
"Attach the drivers of ``devices`` to the elements of ``ctx`` that "
"represent them."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.associate:3 of
msgid "The context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.associate:4 of
msgid "Discovered devices (:func:`discover`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.associate:5 of
msgid ""
"Serial number of the device of each element, by element path, when a "
"model is shared."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.associate:6 of
msgid "Connect the drivers."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.associate:8 of
msgid "The device of each associated element, by path."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.discover:1 of
msgid "Return the devices that answer ``*IDN?``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.discover:3 of
msgid "Addresses ``host:port`` or ``tcp://host:port``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.discover:4 of
msgid ""
"``True`` to try every serial port of the computer, or a list of ports "
"(pyserial URLs)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.discover:5 of
msgid "``True`` to try every VISA resource, or a list of resources."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.discover:6 of
msgid "Time allowed to each candidate to answer, in seconds."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.discovery.identify:1 of
msgid ""
"Ask ``*IDN?`` on ``transport`` (opened and closed here); ``None`` if "
"nothing identifiable answers."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.drivers:1 of
msgid ""
"Drivers of equipment: the LumosLabs drivers and the registry of drivers "
"by model (steps P12.5, P12.9)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.drivers:3 of
msgid ""
":func:`driver_for` returns the driver class of a device model (``\"LL-"
"LS100\"``, or a vendor model). Other packages add drivers with "
":func:`register_driver` or through the ``lumos.drivers`` entry points "
"(:func:`load_plugins`), as described in the guide \"Writing a driver\"."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.drivers.DRIVERS:1 of
msgid "Driver classes by device model."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.drivers.PLUGIN_GROUP:1 of
msgid "``model = \"package.module:DriverClass\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.drivers.PLUGIN_GROUP:3 of
msgid "Entry point group of driver plugins"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.drivers.driver_for:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the driver class of ``model`` (plugins are loaded on the first "
"unknown model)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.drivers.load_plugins:1 of
msgid ""
"Register the drivers of the entry points ``group`` of installed packages;"
" return their models."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.drivers.register_driver:1 of
msgid "Register ``cls`` as the driver of the devices of ``model``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators:1 of
msgid "Emulators of the LumosLabs devices (step P12.4, REQ-HW-3, ADR-0014)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators:3 of
msgid ""
"An emulator answers the LumosLabs protocol "
"(``docs/hardware/lumoslabs_protocol.md``) line by line "
"(:meth:`Emulator.handle`). It runs in the process (through a "
":class:`~lumos.hardware.transport.PipeTransport`) or behind a TCP server "
"(:class:`EmulatorServer`, ``lumos emulators start``), so that the drivers"
" go through a real transport."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.EMULATORS:1 of
msgid "Emulator classes by model."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator:1 of
msgid "Emulated device answering the LumosLabs protocol."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator:3 of
msgid "Serial number."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator:4 of
msgid ""
"Function returning the time in seconds (``time.monotonic``; a fake clock "
"in tests)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator:5 of
msgid "Real time waited before each reply, in seconds."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator:6 of
msgid "Seed of the noise (default: derived from the serial number)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.handle:1 of
msgid ""
"Answer one command line (raises :class:`ConnectionLost` for an injected "
"disconnection)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.inject:1 of
msgid ""
"Inject a fault: ``DISCONNECT``, ``DELAY`` (s), ``OFFSET``, ``STUCK`` or "
"``CLEAR``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.Emulator.now:1 of
msgid "Current time of the device clock."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.quantity:1 of
msgid "Return ``value`` in ``unit`` (a float), or answer ``ERR 101``/``ERR 102``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.check_range:1 of
msgid "Answer ``ERR 200`` if ``value`` (in ``unit``) is outside ``limits[name]``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.offset:1 of
msgid "Offset injected in the measurements."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.start:1 of
msgid ""
"Start a long operation (``ERR 400`` after a stop, ``ERR 300`` if another "
"one runs)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.require_ready:1 of
msgid ""
"Answer ``ERR 400`` after an emergency stop and ``ERR 300`` during an "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.Emulator.busy:1 of
msgid "Whether a long operation is running."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.cmd_star_idn_q:1 of
msgid "``*IDN?``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.cmd_star_rst:1 of
msgid "``*RST``: stop the operation and clear the emergency stop."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.cmd_status_q:1 of
msgid "``STATUS?``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.cmd_busy_q:1 of
msgid "``BUSY?``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.cmd_stop:1 of
msgid "``STOP``: freeze the operation in progress and latch the emergency stop."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.cmd_limits_q:1 of
msgid "``LIMITS? <name>``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.cmd_sim_fault:1 of
msgid "``SIM:FAULT <kind> [value]``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.reset:1 of
msgid "Device-specific part of ``*RST``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.Emulator.halt:1 of
msgid "Device-specific part of ``STOP`` (laser off...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.base.EmulatorError:1 of
msgid "Error answered as ``ERR <code> <message>``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.EmulatorServer:1 of
msgid ""
"TCP server of one emulator (use as a context manager, or :meth:`start` "
"and :meth:`stop`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.EmulatorServer.address:1 of
msgid "``(host, port)`` the server listens on."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.EmulatorServer.start:1 of
msgid "Serve in a background thread."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.EmulatorServer.stop:1 of
msgid "Stop serving."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.hardware.emulators.create_emulator:1 of
msgid ""
"Return an emulator of ``model`` (e.g. ``\"LL-LS100\"``); options as for "
":class:`Emulator`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/index.md:367
msgid "Service layer"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service:1 of
msgid "The service layer of LUMOS (step P13.1, REQ-SVC-1, ADR-0015)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service:3 of
msgid ""
":class:`Service` exposes the high-level operations shared by the web "
"backend and the MCP server: sessions and contexts, editing of the graph, "
"validation, asynchronous runs with progress, inspection of ports, "
"catalogues, archives and the operation of equipment. Its inputs and "
"outputs are typed messages (:mod:`lumos.service.models`) where quantities"
" are written as text (``\"0.5 mm\"``); its errors (:class:`ServiceError`)"
" say what went wrong and how to fix it. The adapters only translate "
"between their protocol and these calls, so that the same request gives "
"the same result in Python, on the web and through an AI assistant."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service:1 of
msgid ""
"Sessions, contexts and operations of LUMOS for the web interface and the "
"MCP server."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service:3 of
msgid "Settings of the deployment (operation, quotas, directories)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.create_session:1 of
msgid ""
"Open a session; its actions are journaled with ``origin`` (``python``, "
"``web`` or ``mcp``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.close_session:1 of
msgid "Close a session, its contexts and the drivers they hold."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.focus:1 of
msgid "Bring ``context`` to the foreground of the session (``None``: no context)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.focus:3 of
msgid ""
"The web interface focuses the context it shows; the tools of an assistant"
" working on the same session use the focused context by default, and the "
"interface follows the contexts they focus."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.revisions:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the revision of every context of the session (cheap: no summary is"
" built)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.get_focus:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the context in the foreground of the session, who focused it and "
"the count of changes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.list_element_types:1 of
msgid "Element types, filtered by words of ``query``, a page at a time."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.get_element_schema:1 of
msgid "JSON Schema of an element type (parameters with units and bounds, ports)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.search_docs:1 of
msgid "Documentation pages matching ``query``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.create_context:1 of
msgid "Create an empty context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.list_contexts:1 of
msgid "Contexts of the session."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.close_context:1 of
msgid "Forget a context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.presets_dir:1 of
msgid "Directory of the preset ``.lumos`` files."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.list_presets:1 of
msgid "Preset contexts."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.load_preset:1 of
msgid "Load a preset into a new context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.import_lumos:1 of
msgid "Create a context from the text (or the mapping) of a ``.lumos`` document."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.export_lumos:1 of
msgid "Return the ``.lumos`` document of a context (JSON text)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.export_python:1 of
msgid "Return the equivalent Python script of a context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.describe_context:1 of
msgid "Elements, values, connections, mode and band of a context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.undo:1 of
msgid "Undo the last edit of a context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.redo:1 of
msgid "Redo the last undone edit of a context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.update_ui:1 of
msgid ""
"Merge ``ui`` into the interface data of a context (positions of the "
"blocks...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.update_ui:3 of
msgid ""
"The library ignores these data; the ``.lumos`` file keeps them. With "
"``record=False`` the change is not an edit of its own for undo (e.g. the "
"placement of a block just added)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.set_context:1 of
msgid ""
"Rename a context, change its description or the seed of its random "
"streams (REQ-CTX-6)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.set_free:1 of
msgid ""
"Mark the parameter ``\"element.field\"`` as free with a prior, or fixed "
"again (REQ-EL-3)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.set_free:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``prior`` is ``{\"kind\": \"uniform\" | \"loguniform\", \"low\": ..., "
"\"high\": ...}`` or ``{\"kind\": \"normal\", \"mean\": ..., \"std\": "
"...}``, values with their units (``\"1 mm\"``). Monte-Carlo runs draw the"
" free parameters from their priors."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.add_element:1 of
msgid ""
"Add an element of ``type_id`` with the given parameter values (``\"2 "
"mW\"``...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.create_group:1 of
msgid "Add a group of elements that behaves as one element (REQ-CTX-7)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.create_group:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``elements`` are ``{\"type\": type_id, \"name\": ..., \"params\": "
"{...}}``, ``connections`` are pairs ``[\"child.port\", \"child.port\"]`` "
"inside the group and ``expose`` maps the names of the ports of the group "
"to internal ports (``{\"out\": \"laser.out\"}``). Nothing is added if any"
" part is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.remove_element:1 of
msgid "Remove an element and its connections."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.connect:1 of
msgid "Connect the output ``source`` to the input ``target`` (``\"id.port\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.disconnect:1 of
msgid "Remove a connection."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.set_param:1 of
msgid ""
"Set a parameter or setting ``\"element.field\"`` (quantities as ``\"5 "
"mm\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.set_observation:1 of
msgid "Set the observation band and its number of wavelengths."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.add_feedback:1 of
msgid ""
"Feed the output ``source`` (``\"id.port\"``) back to the field ``target``"
" of a loop (ADR-0020)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.add_feedback:3 of
msgid ""
"``mode=\"add\"`` adds the value to the field at each step (an "
"integrator), ``\"set\"`` replaces it. Run the loop with :meth:`run_loop`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.build_pipeline:1 of
msgid "Chain processing elements after the output ``source``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.build_pipeline:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each step is ``{\"type\": type_id, \"name\": ..., \"params\": {...}}``; "
"the first input of each element is connected to the first output of the "
"previous one."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.rename_element:1 of
msgid ""
"Rename an element (``\"laser\"`` or ``\"group.child\"``), keeping its "
"connections and position."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.group_elements:1 of
msgid ""
"Move elements of the context into a new group exposing their free ports "
"(REQ-WEB-4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.ungroup:1 of
msgid ""
"Dissolve a group: its elements join the context and keep their "
"connections."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.copy_elements:1 of
msgid ""
"Return a fragment holding ``elements``, the connections between them and "
"their positions."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.paste_elements:1 of
msgid ""
"Add the elements of a fragment (from :meth:`copy_elements`) with free "
"names; return the names."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.export_element:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the ``.lumos`` document of an element or a group (a reusable block"
" for lumos.io)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.import_element:1 of
msgid ""
"Insert the element or group of a ``.lumos`` document (a block), renamed "
"if its name is taken."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.validate_context:1 of
msgid "Problems that would make a run fail, with suggested fixes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.explain_sampling:1 of
msgid ""
"How a propagation element will be computed: method (forced or chosen by "
"the planner) and why."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.plan_propagation:1 of
msgid "Alias of :meth:`explain_sampling`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run:1 of
msgid ""
"Start a run of ``outputs`` in the background; follow it with "
":meth:`get_job`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:1 of
msgid ""
"Start a study in the background: a sweep or a Monte-Carlo run (REQ-"
"CTX-10)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:3 of
msgid ""
"Follow the job with :meth:`get_job`, read its points with "
":meth:`get_study`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:5 of
msgid ""
"``\"sweep\"``: run the context for the values of ``parameters``; "
"``\"sample\"``: Monte-Carlo run of ``n`` draws of the free parameters "
"from their priors (see :meth:`set_free`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:7 of
msgid "Ports to compute at each point (default: the outputs of the context)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:8 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For sweeps, the values of each path ``\"element.field\"``: a list such as"
" ``[\"1 mm\", \"2 mm\"]``, or a range such as ``{\"start\": \"1 mm\", "
"\"stop\": \"5 mm\", \"num\": 5, \"log\": false}``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:10 of
msgid ""
"For sweeps, ``\"grid\"`` (every combination) or ``\"zip\"`` (the i-th "
"values together)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:11 of
msgid "For Monte-Carlo runs, the number of draws."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:12 of
msgid ""
"``\"fixed\"`` (the noise of the context at every point, default of "
"sweeps) or ``\"independent\"`` (a new noise realization per point, "
"default of Monte-Carlo runs)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_study:14 of
msgid ""
"Keep the figure of every drawable output at every point "
"(:meth:`get_recording`); the outputs of ``Recorder`` blocks are recorded "
"anyway."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_loop:1 of
msgid ""
"Run the context as a closed loop of ``steps`` iterations of ``period`` "
"(ADR-0020)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.run_loop:3 of
msgid ""
"At each step the outputs are computed, then the feedbacks are applied and"
" the clock advances. The fields driven by the feedbacks and the clock "
"keep their final values; :meth:`undo` puts them back. Read the steps with"
" :meth:`get_study` (parameter ``time``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.get_recording:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the PNG figure of ``port`` recorded at the point ``point`` of a "
"study (from 0)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.get_study:1 of
msgid ""
"Points of a finished study: values of the parameters, realization, "
"summaries of the outputs."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.study_csv:1 of
msgid "CSV table of a finished study (one row per point)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.default_outputs:1 of
msgid "Return the outputs to run when none is named."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.default_outputs:3 of
msgid ""
"Those listed by the context (``meta.outputs``), else the unconnected "
"outputs of its elements."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.list_jobs:1 of
msgid "Return the runs of the session, oldest first."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.cancel_job:1 of
msgid ""
"Ask a queued or running run to stop (at the end of the element being "
"computed)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.get_job:1 of
msgid "Status, progress and outcome of a run."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.wait_job:1 of
msgid "Wait for the end of a run (or ``timeout`` seconds)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.get_result:1 of
msgid "Summary of an output computed by a run."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.inspect_port:1 of
msgid ""
"Compute (or reuse) the signal of an output port and summarise it, with a "
"figure."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.port_file:1 of
msgid ""
"Compute the signal of ``port`` and return it as a file: ``png``, ``plt``,"
" ``npz`` or ``json``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.result_file:1 of
msgid ""
"Return an output computed by a run as a file (see :meth:`port_file`), "
"without computing again."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.radial_profile:1 of
msgid ""
"Azimuthal mean of the intensity of a field at ``port``, in rings of width"
" ``bin_width``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.radial_profile:3 of
msgid ""
"``center`` is ``[x, y]`` (default: the origin of the grid); "
"``normalize=\"peak\"`` divides by the maximum of the intensity, which "
"gives contrasts. Radii are the middles of the rings, in SI units of the "
"grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.journal:1 of
msgid ""
"Last entries of the journal of a context (``kind``: ``\"action\"``, "
"``\"log\"``...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.journal_since:1 of
msgid ""
"Entries of the journal of a context from index ``start`` (to follow it as"
" it grows)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.resolve_object:1 of
msgid ""
"Typed record of an astronomical object, with the provenance of every "
"field."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.evaluate_detection:1 of
msgid ""
"Contrast curve (detection limit versus separation) of the residual image "
"of ``port``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.archive_root:1 of
msgid "Directory of the archives of the runs."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.list_archives:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the archives of the runs, most recent first (those of ``session`` "
"with session storage)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.storage:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the disk used by the data of ``session``, its limit, the free disk"
" and the warnings."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.archive_zip:1 of
msgid ""
"Return an archive of the archive directory as the bytes of a ``.zip`` "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.read_archive_metadata:1 of
msgid ""
"``metadata.yml`` of an archive (only inside the archive directory of the "
"service or session)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.discover_devices:1 of
msgid "Devices answering on the given connections (operation must be enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.associate_devices:1 of
msgid ""
"Attach and connect the drivers of the discovered devices to the elements "
"of a context."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.list_devices:1 of
msgid "Drivers attached to the elements of a context, with their state."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.device_status:1 of
msgid "State of the driver of an element."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.confirmation_needed:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the device that an action of ``element`` would drive, if it needs "
"a human confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.confirmation_needed:3 of
msgid ""
"``None`` when the action only changes the simulation, or when the "
"operation is disabled (the action is then refused by "
":meth:`execute_action`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.execute_action:1 of
msgid ""
"Execute an action of an element; on equipment, only when enabled and "
"confirmed by a human."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.stop_all:1 of
msgid "Emergency stop of every device of a context (always allowed)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.service.Service.shutdown:1 of
msgid "Close every session and stop the workers."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models:1 of
msgid ""
"Typed messages of the service layer (Pydantic models, step P13.1, "
"ADR-0015)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models:3 of
msgid ""
"Every value with a unit is written as a string ``\"<value> <unit>\"`` "
"(``\"0.5 mm\"``), so that the messages read well in JSON, in the web "
"interface and in the answers of an AI assistant."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.ActionResult:1 of
msgid ""
"Outcome of an action: mode, predicted and measured durations, returned "
"value."
msgstr ""

