#: lumos.service.models.ArchiveInfo:1 of
msgid "An archive of a run."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.ConnectionInfo:1 of
msgid "A connection ``source`` (``\"id.port\"``) → ``target``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.ContextSummary:1 of
msgid "A context: its elements, connections, mode and observation band."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.DeviceModel:1 of
msgid "A discovered device."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.DocHit:1 of
msgid "A documentation page matching a search."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.ElementSummary:1 of
msgid "An element of a context, with its values in their units."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.ElementTypeInfo:1 of
msgid "An element type of the registry."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.FeedbackInfo:1 of
msgid ""
"A feedback of a loop: the port ``source`` drives the field ``target`` "
"(``mode`` ``set`` or ``add``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.FocusInfo:1 of
msgid ""
"The context in the foreground of a session, shared by the web interface "
"and the assistant (P14.18)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.FocusInfo:3 of
msgid ""
"``origin`` tells who focused it last (``web``, ``mcp`` or ``python``); "
"``count`` grows at every change of the focus, so that a client sees a "
"change even when the same context comes back."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.GroupInfo:1 of
msgid ""
"The inside of a group: connections of its elements and exposed ports "
"(``port: \"child.port\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.Issue:1 of
msgid "A problem found in a context, with a suggested fix."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.JobInfo:1 of
msgid ""
"A run or a study: its status (``queued``, ``running``, ``done``, "
"``failed``), progress and outputs."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.Page:1 of
msgid "One page of a long list."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.PortFile:1 of
msgid "A file made from the signal of a port: its name, media type and content."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.PortSummary:1 of
msgid ""
"Compact description of a signal: kind, unit, shape, a few values, "
"statistics, optional figure."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.PresetInfo:1 of
msgid ""
"A preset context: file name, title, description, outputs and the types of"
" its elements."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.ServiceConfig:1 of
msgid "Configuration of a service (deployment profiles set it, step P14.3)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.SessionInfo:1 of
msgid ""
"A session: its identifier and the origin of its actions (``python``, "
"``web`` or ``mcp``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.StorageInfo:1 of
msgid ""
"Disk used by the data of a session (archives, recordings), its limit and "
"the free disk (P14.21)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.StudyPoint:1 of
msgid ""
"A point of a study: values of the parameters, noise realization and "
"summaries of the outputs."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.models.StudyResult:1 of
msgid ""
"The points of a sweep or of a Monte-Carlo run, or the steps of a loop "
"(parameter ``time``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.errors:1 of
msgid ""
"Errors of the service layer: a cause and a suggested fix, readable by "
"people and by AI assistants."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.errors.ServiceError:1 of
msgid "An operation of the service failed."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.errors.ServiceError:3 of
msgid "What went wrong."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.errors.ServiceError:4 of
msgid "How to fix it."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.service.errors.ServiceError:5 of
msgid ""
"Category: ``\"invalid\"``, ``\"not_found\"``, ``\"forbidden\"``, "
"``\"quota\"``, ``\"failed\"``."
msgstr ""

