#: ../../api/index.md:380
msgid "MCP server"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp:1 of
msgid "MCP server of LUMOS, for AI assistants (phase 13, REQ-MCP-1, ADR-0016)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp:3 of
msgid ""
"``lumos mcp`` serves it over stdio, ``lumos mcp --transport http`` over "
"streamable HTTP; :func:`create_server` builds it and "
":func:`create_http_app` gives its ASGI application, to mount in a web "
"server. It needs the extra ``mcp`` (``pip install \"lumos-"
"maxima[mcp]\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_server:1 of
msgid "Create the MCP server of LUMOS."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_server:3 of
msgid "Service layer to use (a new one with ``config`` by default)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_server:4 of
msgid "Configuration of the new service (operation, quotas, directories)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_server:5 of
msgid "Name of the server announced to the clients."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_server:6 of
msgid ""
"Existing session of ``service`` to work in (the web instance gives the "
"session of the browser, so that the assistant sees the contexts of the "
"interface); a new session of origin ``mcp`` by default."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_server:8 of
msgid ""
"Whether the user may drive real equipment (operators); otherwise actions "
"reach simulated elements."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_server:9 of
msgid ""
"Gives the URL opening a context of the session in the web interface (tool"
" ``get_view_link``); ``None`` for a server without web interface (stdio)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_server:12 of
msgid "Server to run over stdio (``server.run(\"stdio\")``) or HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_http_app:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the ASGI application serving ``server`` over streamable HTTP at "
"``path`` (step P13.6)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.server.create_http_app:3 of
msgid ""
"The web backend mounts this application (P14), which then adds the "
"authentication of its users; until then, serve it on the local machine "
"only. ``host`` sets the protection against DNS rebinding: requests must "
"name a local host when it is a loopback address."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation:1 of
msgid ""
"Evaluation of the MCP server on typical scenarios (step P13.8, REQ-MCP-7,"
" ADR-0017)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation:3 of
msgid ""
"Each :class:`Scenario` is a task given to an assistant in plain language "
"(use cases UC1, UC8 and UC9 of the requirements), with expected values "
"derived from analytic solutions and a check of the final answer. The "
"assistant ends its answer with a JSON object holding the requested "
"values; :func:`parse_answer` reads it."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation:7 of
msgid ""
":func:`run_reference` solves a scenario with a scripted sequence of MCP "
"tool calls. It runs in the tests: it proves that the scenario can be "
"solved with the tools, and that the checks accept a right answer."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation:9 of
msgid ""
":func:`run_with_claude_code` gives the task to Claude Code (``claude "
"-p``, the subscription of the user, no API key) with the tools of the "
"server, and checks its answer. ``tools/mcp_eval.py --claude-code`` runs "
"it on demand."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.SCENARIOS:1 of
msgid "Scenarios of the evaluation, by name."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.EvaluationResult:1 of
msgid ""
"Outcome of a scenario: the answer, what is wrong with it, and the final "
"text of the assistant."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.EvaluationResult.passed:1 of
msgid "Whether the answer is right."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario:1 of
msgid "A task for an assistant with a verifiable expected result."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario:3 of
msgid "Identifier of the scenario."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario:5 of
msgid "Use case of the requirements (``\"UC1\"``...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario:7 of
msgid "Short title."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario:9 of
msgid "What the assistant is asked, ending with the keys of the JSON answer."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario:11 of
msgid "Expected value of each key of the answer."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario:13 of
msgid ""
"How each value is checked: ``(\"rel\", r)`` relative tolerance, "
"``(\"abs\", a)`` absolute tolerance, ``(\"below\", m)`` upper bound (the "
"expected value is then the ideal one)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario:16 of
msgid ""
"Scripted solution: an async function of an MCP client returning the "
"answer."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario.answer_keys:1 of
msgid "Keys of the JSON answer."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.Scenario.check:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the reasons why ``answer`` is wrong (an empty list when it is "
"right)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.claude_code_command:1 of
msgid ""
"Command running Claude Code on ``scenario`` with the MCP server of LUMOS "
"as its only tools."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.claude_code_command:3 of
msgid ""
"The server is started with the current Python interpreter (``python -m "
"lumos.cli mcp``), so it does not depend on the ``PATH``; ``--strict-mcp-"
"config`` ignores the other MCP servers of the user and ``--allowedTools "
"mcp__lumos`` lets Claude Code call the tools of LUMOS without asking."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.parse_answer:1 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Return the last JSON object written in ``text`` (the final answer of an "
"assistant), or ``{}``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.run_reference:1 of
msgid ""
"Solve ``scenario`` with its scripted tool calls through ``client`` and "
"check the answer."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.run_with_claude_code:1 of
msgid ""
"Give ``scenario`` to Claude Code (``claude -p``) with the tools of LUMOS "
"and check its answer."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.mcp.evaluation.run_with_claude_code:3 of
msgid ""
"Claude Code runs with the account of the user (a Claude subscription, no "
"API key). ``run`` replaces :func:`subprocess.run` in the tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/index.md:393
msgid "Web backend"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web:1 of
msgid ""
"Web interface of LUMOS: the FastAPI backend serving the visual editor "
"(phase 14, ADR-0018)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web:3 of
msgid ""
":func:`create_app`: the ASGI application, a thin adapter of the service "
"layer (:mod:`lumos.service`);"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web:4 of
msgid ":class:`WebConfig`: profile, hosts and quotas of an instance."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web:6 of
msgid ""
"Serve it with ``lumos web`` (``localhost:8000`` by default). Needs the "
"extra ``web``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.app.create_app:1 of
msgid "Create the web application of LUMOS."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.app.create_app:3 of
msgid ""
"Settings of the instance (profile, hosts, users, quotas of the "
"service...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.app.create_app:4 of
msgid "Service layer to use; by default a new one built from ``config.service``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.app.create_app:6 of
msgid "The ASGI application, to serve with ``uvicorn`` (``lumos web`` does it)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.app.create_app:9 of
msgid "The configuration is unsafe (see :meth:`WebConfig.check`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config:1 of
msgid ""
"Configuration of the web instance (steps P14.1 to P14.3, REQ-WEB-9, REQ-"
"WEB-10, ADR-0019)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config:3 of
msgid "Two profiles:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config:5 of
msgid ""
"``local``: one user on their own machine. The server listens on "
"``localhost`` only; its user has every role (the operation of equipment, "
"when enabled, still asks a confirmation for each action)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config:7 of
msgid ""
"``public``: anyone on the internet. Visitors are anonymous simulators by "
"default, with tight quotas; the operation of equipment is disabled and "
"can only be enabled together with TLS and registered operators."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.LOOPBACK_HOSTS:1 of
msgid "Host names of the local machine."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.PROFILE_DEFAULTS:1 of
msgid "Settings that depend on the profile when they are not given."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.ConfigError:1 of
msgid "A configuration of the web instance is invalid or unsafe."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.WebConfig:1 of
msgid "Settings of a web instance of LUMOS."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.WebConfig:3 of
msgid ""
"Settings left out take the default of the profile "
"(:data:`PROFILE_DEFAULTS`; on a public instance, the quotas of the "
"service of ``PUBLIC_SERVICE_DEFAULTS`` too)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.WebConfig.local_only:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether the instance only serves its own machine (local profile on a "
"loopback address)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.WebConfig.tls:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether requests reach the instance over TLS (certificate, or a proxy "
"terminating TLS)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.WebConfig.check:1 of
msgid "Refuse unsafe combinations of settings."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.WebConfig.check:3 of
msgid ""
"The local profile on a non-local address; the operation of equipment "
"outside the local machine     without TLS, without a registered operator "
"or with anonymous operators; a missing users file."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.load_config:1 of
msgid ""
"Read a TOML configuration file (sections at the top level and "
"``[service]``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.load_config:3 of
msgid ""
"TOML file, e.g. ``profile = \"public\"``, ``users_file = "
"\"users.toml\"``, ``[service] max_run_seconds = 30``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.load_config:5 of
msgid "Settings given on the command line; they win over the file."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.config.load_config:7 of
msgid "The file is not valid TOML or has unknown or invalid settings."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth:1 of
msgid ""
"Users, passwords and SSH keys of a web instance (step P14.2, REQ-WEB-9, "
"ADR-0019)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth:3 of
msgid "Passwords are stored as Argon2id hashes (``argon2-cffi``), never in clear."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth:4 of
msgid ""
"An SSH key proves its owner by signing a challenge of the server in the "
"SSHSIG format of OpenSSH (``ssh-keygen -Y sign -n lumos``), verified here"
" with ``cryptography``. Ed25519, ECDSA (NIST P-256, P-384, P-521) and RSA"
" keys (signatures ``rsa-sha2-256`` and ``rsa-sha2-512``) are accepted."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth:7 of
msgid "Users are listed in a TOML file managed with ``lumos users``::"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.ROLES:1 of
msgid "Roles, from the least to the most privileged."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.User:1 of
msgid "A registered user."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.User:3 of
msgid "User name."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.User:5 of
msgid "``\"viewer\"``, ``\"simulator\"`` or ``\"operator\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.User:7 of
msgid "Argon2id hash of the password, if the user logs in with one."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.User:9 of
msgid "Public keys (lines of ``id_*.pub``) the user logs in with."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.hash_password:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the Argon2id hash of ``password`` (``argon2-cffi`` parameters, RFC"
" 9106 low-memory profile)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.load_users:1 of
msgid "Read a users file."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.load_users:3 of
msgid ""
"Missing or invalid file, unknown role or setting, password not given as "
"an Argon2id hash."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.role_allows:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether ``role`` has the rights of ``needed`` (each role includes the "
"rights of the previous ones)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.save_users:1 of
msgid "Write a users file."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.verify_password:1 of
msgid "Whether ``password`` matches the Argon2id hash ``hashed``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.verify_ssh_signature:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether ``signature`` (SSHSIG, from ``ssh-keygen -Y sign``) signs "
"``message`` with ``public_key``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.verify_ssh_signature:3 of
msgid "Line of an OpenSSH public key file (``ssh-ed25519 AAAA... comment``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.verify_ssh_signature:4 of
msgid "The signed bytes (the challenge of the server)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.verify_ssh_signature:5 of
msgid "Armored signature (``-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----`` ...)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.auth.verify_ssh_signature:6 of
msgid ""
"Namespace the signature must have been made for (``-n`` of ``ssh-"
"keygen``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login:1 of
msgid ""
"``lumos login``: log in to a web instance with an SSH key (step P14.2, "
"REQ-WEB-9)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login:3 of
msgid ""
"The server sends a challenge; OpenSSH signs it (``ssh-keygen -Y sign -n "
"lumos``, which uses the SSH agent for keys protected by a passphrase); "
"the server checks the signature against the public keys of the user and "
"answers with a session token, usable as ``Authorization: Bearer "
"<token>``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login.LoginError:1 of
msgid "The login failed (server refusal, missing ssh-keygen, unreadable key)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login.login:1 of
msgid ""
"Log in to the instance at ``url`` as ``user`` with an SSH key and return "
"the session token."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login.login:3 of
msgid "Base URL of the instance, e.g. ``https://lumos.example.org``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login.login:4 of
msgid "User name registered on the instance."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login.login:5 of
msgid ""
"Private key file (``~/.ssh/id_ed25519``), or its public key when the "
"private key is in the SSH agent."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login.login:6 of
msgid ""
"HTTP client with ``post`` (``httpx.Client``); by default a new one with "
"TLS verification."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login.sign_challenge:1 of
msgid ""
"Sign ``challenge`` with the private key ``key`` (or its ``.pub`` file "
"with an SSH agent)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.login.sign_challenge:3 of
msgid "The armored SSHSIG signature written by ``ssh-keygen -Y sign``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security:1 of
msgid ""
"Rate limits, audit journal and transport checks of a web instance (step "
"P14.2, REQ-WEB-9, ADR-0019)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.AuditLog:1 of
msgid ""
"Journal of the security events: one JSON object per line, also sent to "
"the logger ``lumos.audit``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.AuditLog:3 of
msgid "Entries never hold passwords, signatures or session tokens."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.AuditLog:5 of
msgid "JSON-lines file, or ``None`` for the logger only."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.AuditLog.record:1 of
msgid ""
"Append an event (``login``, ``logout``, ``forbidden``, ``action``...) and"
" its outcome."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.RateLimiter:1 of
msgid ""
"At most ``limit`` events per key in any window of ``window`` seconds "
"(sliding window)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.RateLimiter:3 of
msgid "Events allowed per window; ``None`` allows everything."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.RateLimiter:4 of
msgid "Length of the window in seconds."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.RateLimiter.hit:1 of
msgid ""
"Record an event of ``key``; return 0 if allowed, else the seconds to wait"
" before the next one."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.client_address:1 of
msgid ""
"Address of the client: the first ``X-Forwarded-For`` entry behind a "
"trusted proxy, else the peer."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.web.security.is_secure:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether the request came over TLS (directly, or through a trusted proxy "
"terminating TLS)."
msgstr ""

